Tea-cup 茶杯 ch''a-pui', 'Water水shui''|Bring□一嚟,來ning—lai,(or)loiTea茶ch''a|Do.拈一嚟,來nim—lai,(or)loiIorme我ngo''|Do.攞*lo''You你ni''|Givemetea俾茶我pi''ch''ango''Have有yau''|Towant(like)要,愛iu''(or)oi''Give俾pi''|Interrog.particlesatendofaquestion.啞,呢,ā,ni,me,mo'',andmo(moonlyfollowsyau;itiscontractionof''myan.)Sugar(white)白糖pak-t''ongBread麵飽min''-pauTea-cup茶杯ch''a-pui', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-018-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 18, 1, NULL, 'The interrogative particles are respectively used rather in observance of custom than because of any marked difference in value, though MO seems more generally than the others to imply a belief on the part of the speaker that the answer will be affirmative. Two are sometimes used together.

There being no case inflections in Chinese, the same word answers for I or me, according to its place in the sentence. Thus "I give" is NGO PI 我俾 "give me" is PI NGO 俾我.

There is, strictly speaking, no article* in Chinese though the numeral "one" or a demonstrative pronoun frequently supplies its place.

The mood and tenses of verbs are not marked by inflections, particles being used in their place.

In ordinary colloquial, the copulative conjunction is often replaced by the verb when several nouns are coupled as, what we should term, nominatives or accusatives of a verb. Thus: give me tea sugar and milk may be translated, give tea, give sugar, give milk, me.

The word bring is, literally, carry come (NING LOI 擰來) in Chinese. Take away is, similarly, carry go, as will be seen hereafter.

In the following sentences words in brackets are not expressed in the Chinese. With the exception of the article they will be so marked in this and the two following lessons.

1 Bring (some) bread 擰麵飽來 ning min-pau loi

2 Bring (some) water 擰水來 ning shui loi

3 Bring me (some) tea 擰茶來我 ning ch''a loi ngo

4 Bring a tea-cup 擰茶杯來 ning ch''a-pui loi

5 Give me sugar 俾白糖我 pi pak-t''ong ngo

6 Have you (any) sugar? 你有白糖冇呀 ni yau pak-t''ong mo à?

7 I have sugar 我有白糖 ngo yau pak-t''ong

8 Give me tea (and) sugar 俾茶俾白糖我 pi ch''a, pi pak-t''ong ngo

9 Give me bread (and) water 俾麵飽俾水我 pi min-pau, pi shui ngo

10 Bring sugar (and) water 擰白糖擰水來 ning pak-t''ong, ning shui loi

11 Have you tea? 你有茶呢 ni yau ch''a ni?

12 I have tea 我有茶 ngo yau ch''a

13 Have you water? 你有水麽 ni yau shui mo ?

14 I have sugar 我有白糖 ngo yau pak-t''ong

15 Have you (any) bread? 你有麵飽呀 ni yau min-pau à?

16 I have tea-cups 我有茶杯 ngo yau ch''a-pui

17 Give me tea-cups 俾茶杯我 pi ch''a-pui ngo

18 Give me water, sugar (and) 俾水,俾白糖,俾茶 pi shui, pi pak-t''ong, pi ch''a,

tea 我 ngo

