  ('cvh-030-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 30, 1, NULL, 'Cap or hat 頂帽 (teng'') mo'' To put away收埋,擠 shau mai, tsai

To put on clothes 着衣服 cheuk i fuk埋 mai

To put on a hat 戴帽 tai mo'' To (lit. to pass 過 kwo''

Box 箱 seung over)

Lookiug glass 面鏡 min` keng'' To be able, can 得，能 tāk, nang

Ch''ü 處, place, is often added at the end of sentences indicating locality; e.g HAI T''OI MIN CH''ü 喺檯面處, it is on the table. PI TSAU 啤酒 like many other compounds, such as KA LI 咖喱 curry, KA FEI 咖啡 coffee &c. are bastard words intended to express the foreign sound of the article named. Several such words are unavoidably introduced in these exercises, on account of their being current amongst native servants. I FOOK 衣服 means clothes generally; KO KIN SHAM 响件衫 the coat and visible parts of a suit.

1 One bottle of beer 一樽啤酒 yat tsun pi tsau

2 I waut to put on clothes 要着衣服 iu cheuk i fook

3 Where is the comb? 梳係邊處 sho hai pin ch''ü?

4 It is on the looking glass 在鏡面處 tsoi keng min ch''ü

5 Brush my boots 擦我對靴 ts''at ngo tui hö

6 Take off your clothes 除衣服 ch''ü i fook

7 Bring my slippers 拈我對撻□鞋來 nim ngo tui t''at tsang hai loi

8 Put away my boots 擠埋我對靴 tsai mai ngo tui hö

9 Have you good boots? 你有好靴冇 ni yau ho hö mo?

10 How many table napkins 你有幾多條茶巾 ni yau ki to t''iu ch''a kān?

have you?

11 I have six 我有六條 ngo yau luk t''iu

12 Put them in the box 擠入箱喇 tsai yap seung la

13 Put away my coat 擠埋我件衫 tsai mai ngo kin sham

14 Do you want a stick? 你要鞭杆唔要 ni iu pin kon ''m iu

15 Where is my hat? 我頂帽係邊處 ngo teng mo hai pin ch''ü?

16 Here it is on the table 係檯面處 hai t''oi min ch''ü

17 Please give it me 請你俾過我 ts''ing ni pi kwo ngo

18 Tell the house-coolie to brush 叫管店擦我對靴 kiu kun-tim ts''at ngo tui hö my hoots

19 Bring soda water 拈嗝囒水來 nim ho-lan-shui loi

20 Get my shoes and clothes 拈我對鞋及衣服來 nim ngo tui hai kap i fook loi', 'Caporhat頂帽(teng'')mo''Toputaway收埋,擠shaumai,tsaiToputonclothes着衣服cheukifuk埋maiToputonahat戴帽taimo''To(lit.topass過kwo''Box箱seungover)Lookiugglass面鏡min`keng''Tobeable,can得，能tāk,nangCh''ü處,place,isoftenaddedattheendofsentencesindicatinglocality;e.gHAIT''OIMINCH''ü喺檯面處,itisonthetable.PITSAU啤酒likemanyothercompounds,suchasKALI咖喱curry,KAFEI咖啡coffee&c.arebastardwordsintendedtoexpresstheforeignsoundofthearticlenamed.Severalsuchwordsareunavoidablyintroducedintheseexercises,onaccountoftheirbeingcurrentamongstnativeservants.IFOOK衣服meansclothesgenerally;KOKINSHAM响件衫thecoatandvisiblepartsofasuit.1Onebottleofbeer一樽啤酒yattsunpitsau2Iwauttoputonclothes要着衣服iucheukifook3Whereisthecomb?梳係邊處shohaipinch''ü?4Itisonthelookingglass在鏡面處tsoikengminch''ü5Brushmyboots擦我對靴ts''atngotuihö6Takeoffyourclothes除衣服ch''üifook7Bringmyslippers拈我對撻□鞋來nimngotuit''attsanghailoi8Putawaymyboots擠埋我對靴tsaimaingotuihö9Haveyougoodboots?你有好靴冇niyauhohömo?10Howmanytablenapkins你有幾多條茶巾niyaukitot''iuch''akān?haveyou?11Ihavesix我有六條ngoyaulukt''iu12Puttheminthebox擠入箱喇tsaiyapseungla13Putawaymycoat擠埋我件衫tsaimaingokinsham14Doyouwantastick?你要鞭杆唔要niiupinkon''miu15Whereismyhat?我頂帽係邊處ngotengmohaipinch''ü?16Hereitisonthetable係檯面處hait''oiminch''ü17Pleasegiveitme請你俾過我ts''ingnipikwongo18Tellthehouse-coolietobrush叫管店擦我對靴kiukun-timts''atngotuihömyhoots19Bringsodawater拈嗝囒水來nimho-lan-shuiloi20Getmyshoesandclothes拈我對鞋及衣服來nimngotuihaikapifookloi', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-031-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 31, 1, NULL, '21 Put away that beer 擠埋响啲啤酒 tsai mai ko ti pi tsau

