INSERT INTO articles (id, corpus, issue, issue_date, page, seq, title, text, text_norm, status) VALUES
  ('cvh-032-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 32, 1, NULL, 'It will be seen that compound words are not unfrequent, and that the monosyllabic character of the spoken language is by no means so strongly marked as is sometimes imagined. All compound words are hyphened in these exercises.

The particle ti 的 before a noun signifies some, a little.

The word tso做to do or make, is often added to other verbs as an intensive particle; e.g. It is called "to," KIU tso to叫做刀.

曉 hiu, to understand, "to know how to" is often used in place of ui 噲, where in English we should use the words can, to be able: e.g. Can you write? NI hiu se tsz mo? 你曉寫字麽.

1 Don''t take away that ink 唔好拈个的墨水去 ''m ho nim ko-ti mäk-shui hü

2 Very well, I will put it here 好咯; 我放在呢處 ho lok, ngo fong tsoi ni ch''ü

3 Bring ink, I want to write 拈墨水來,我要寫字 nim măk-shui loi, ngo iu se tsz

4 Put the candle on the table 放蠟燭在檯面 fong lap-chuk tsoi t''oi min

5 Light the lamp 點個盞燈 tim ko chän-täng

6 Bring a pen and an ink-slab 拈筆墨硯來 nim pät măk-in loi

7 Rub me some ink 磨的墨我 moh ti măk ngo

8 Get a pair of scissors and cut拈把鉸剪來,剪個 nim pa kau-tsin loi, tsin ko t''iu that handkerchief 條手巾 shau-kän

9 Get me a handkerchief and 拈條手巾,拈把遮來 nim t''iu shau-kän, nim pa che loi my umhrella 我 ngo

10 Light the candle and take it 點蠟燭拈上去 tim lap chuk, nim sheung hui up-stairs

11 Brush my trowers 擦我條褲 ts''at ngo t''iu fu

12 Where are the needle and thread? 個眼針線喺邊處 ko ngan chām, sin hai pin ch''ü?

13 It is down-stairs 喺下低 hai ha tai

14 Get me a pin and the scis-拈大頭針,拈鉸剪 nim tai t''au chām, nim kau-tsin sors 來我 loi ngo

15 Fetch the lantern 拈手燈來我 nim shau täng loi ngo

16 Have you a penknife 你有刀仔冇 ni yau to-tsai mo?

17 No! but I have a pencil 冇! 我有鉛筆 mo! ngo yau ün-pät

18 What is this called? 呢的叫乜野 ni ti kiu mät-ye?

19 It is called a penknife 叫做刀仔 kiu tso to-tsai

20 Can you write characters? 你曉寫字麽 ni hiu se tsz moh?

21 I cannot write characters 我唔噲寫字 ngo ''m ui se tsz', 'Itwillbeseenthatcompoundwordsarenotunfrequent,andthatthemonosyllabiccharacterofthespokenlanguageisbynomeanssostronglymarkedasissometimesimagined.Allcompoundwordsarehyphenedintheseexercises.Theparticleti的beforeanounsignifiessome,alittle.Thewordtso做todoormake,isoftenaddedtootherverbsasanintensiveparticle;e.g.Itiscalled"to,"KIUtsoto叫做刀.曉hiu,tounderstand,"toknowhowto"isoftenusedinplaceofui噲,whereinEnglishweshouldusethewordscan,tobeable:e.g.Canyouwrite?NIhiusetszmo?你曉寫字麽.1Don''ttakeawaythatink唔好拈个的墨水去''mhonimko-timäk-shuihü2Verywell,Iwillputithere好咯;我放在呢處holok,ngofongtsoinich''ü3Bringink,Iwanttowrite拈墨水來,我要寫字nimmăk-shuiloi,ngoiusetsz4Putthecandleonthetable放蠟燭在檯面fonglap-chuktsoit''oimin5Lightthelamp點個盞燈timkochän-täng6Bringapenandanink-slab拈筆墨硯來nimpätmăk-inloi7Rubmesomeink磨的墨我mohtimăkngo8Getapairofscissorsandcut拈把鉸剪來,剪個nimpakau-tsinloi,tsinkot''iuthathandkerchief條手巾shau-kän9Getmeahandkerchiefand拈條手巾,拈把遮來nimt''iushau-kän,nimpacheloimyumhrella我ngo10Lightthecandleandtakeit點蠟燭拈上去timlapchuk,nimsheunghuiup-stairs11Brushmytrowers擦我條褲ts''atngot''iufu12Wherearetheneedleandthread?個眼針線喺邊處konganchām,sinhaipinch''ü?13Itisdown-stairs喺下低haihatai14Getmeapinandthescis-拈大頭針,拈鉸剪nimtait''auchām,nimkau-tsinsors來我loingo15Fetchthelantern拈手燈來我nimshautängloingo16Haveyouapenknife你有刀仔冇niyauto-tsaimo?17No!butIhaveapencil冇!我有鉛筆mo!ngoyauün-pät18Whatisthiscalled?呢的叫乜野nitikiumät-ye?19Itiscalledapenknife叫做刀仔kiutsoto-tsai20Canyouwritecharacters?你曉寫字麽nihiusetszmoh?21Icannotwritecharacters我唔噲寫字ngo''muisetsz', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-033-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 33, 1, NULL, '22 Come (lit. go) with me; fetch the lantern 同我去;拈手燈黎 t''ung ngo hü; nim shau-tang lai

23 Where are my coat, boots and cap? 我件衫,我對靴,我頂帽喺邊處呢 ngo kin sham, ngo tui hö, ngo teng mo, hai pin ch''ü ni

24 They are put away 擠埋喳 tsai mai cha

25 Bring me a bottle of soda-water 拈一樽嗬囒水來我 nim yat tsun ho-lan-shui loi ngo

26 I want a pencil to write characters 我要一枝筆寫字 ngo iu yat chi pāt se tsz

27 Get paper, pens, ink, and an ink-slab 拈紙筆墨水,及墨硯黎 nim chi, păt, mük-shui kap māk-in, lai

28 Sweep the floor; that will do! 掃樓板,好咯 so lau-pan; ho lok!

29 Where is my penknife? 我張刀仔喺邊處呢 ngo cheung to-tsai hai pin ch''ü ni?

30 Cut the handkerchief with the scissors 使較剪剪手巾 shai kau-tsin tsin shau-kān

31 Put on your trowsers and coat 着褲着衫 cheuk fu, cheuk sham

32 Get my book and stick 拈我簿書及我枝鞭杆來 nim ngo po shü, kap ngo chi pin-kon loi', '22Come(lit.go)withme;fetchthelantern同我去;拈手燈黎t''ungngohü;nimshau-tanglai23Wherearemycoat,bootsandcap?我件衫,我對靴,我頂帽喺邊處呢ngokinsham,ngotuihö,ngotengmo,haipinch''üni24Theyareputaway擠埋喳tsaimaicha25Bringmeabottleofsoda-water拈一樽嗬囒水來我nimyattsunho-lan-shuiloingo26Iwantapenciltowritecharacters我要一枝筆寫字ngoiuyatchipātsetsz27Getpaper,pens,ink,andanink-slab拈紙筆墨水,及墨硯黎nimchi,păt,mük-shuikapmāk-in,lai28Sweepthefloor;thatwilldo!掃樓板,好咯solau-pan;holok!29Whereismypenknife?我張刀仔喺邊處呢ngocheungto-tsaihaipinch''üni?30Cutthehandkerchiefwiththescissors使較剪剪手巾shaikau-tsintsinshau-kān31Putonyourtrowsersandcoat着褲着衫cheukfu,cheuksham32Getmybookandstick拈我簿書及我枝鞭杆來nimngoposhü,kapngochipin-konloi', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-033-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 33, 2, 'LESSON X.', 'Chinese (adj.) 唐人嘅 t''ong yan ke'' Bell 鐘 chung

