  ('cvh-042-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 42, 1, NULL, 'Iron 鐵 t''it Flowers 花 fa

Banana 蕉 tsiu To gather flowers 摘花 chak fa

Custard Apple 番荔枝 fan lai''-chi To plant 種 chung''

Lychee 荔枝 lai''-chi A ten cent piece 一個豪子 yat ko ho-tsz''

Whampee 黃皮 wong-p''i Thing 野 ye''

Orange (small) 桔仔,柑 kut-tsai, kom, Dollar 銀錢 ngān-ts''in

Coolie orange 橙 ch''ang

To smoke tobacco is literally "eat smoke,"—an expression to be found in some other languages also.

Rice, as given above, refers to the cooked grain.

And may be rendered by 共 KUNG when coupling substantives, 零 LING being used between numerals. Neither, however, is very frequently used.

1 Boil some rice directly 即刻煲飯 tsik hak po fan

2 Have you any cigars to sell? 你有呂宋烟賣冇 ni yau lu-sung-in mai mo?

3 I want to buy a pipe 我要買枝烟筒 ngo iu mai chi in-t''ung

4 Do you smoke tobacco? 你食烟唔食 ni shik in ''m shik?

5 I like bananas and custard apples 我愛蕉共番荔枝 ngo oi tsiu kung fan lai-chi

6 The lychees are good, the whampees bad 荔枝好黃皮唔好 lai-chi ho, wong-p''i ''m ho

7 Get me fifty oranges (small) 拈五十個桔仔來我 nim ''ng shap ko kăt-tsai loi ngo

8 Boil the sausage 烚個啲釀腸 shăp ko ti yeung-ch''eung

9 Take away those shrimps 拈個啲蝦去 nim ko ti ha hü

10 Do you like to gather flowers? 你愛摘花唔愛 ni oi chak fa ''m oi?

11 Go and plant those vegetables 去種個啲菜 hü chung ko ti ts''oi

12 This is a silver watch 呢個時晨鏢係銀嘅 ni ko shi-shān-piu hai ngān ke

13 That is a copper bell 個啲鐘銅嘅 ko ti chung t''ung ke

14 I want to buy an iron cork-screw 我要買個鐵酒鑽 ngo iu mai ko t''it tsau-tsün

15 What is this thing? 呢的係乜野 ni ti hai māt ye?

16 It is an iron saucepan 係鐵鑊 hai t''it wok

17 All are here 喊嘭哈喺處 ham-pang-lang hai ch''ü', 'Iron鐵t''itFlowers花faBanana蕉tsiuTogatherflowers摘花chakfaCustardApple番荔枝fanlai''-chiToplant種chung''Lychee荔枝lai''-chiAtencentpiece一個豪子yatkoho-tsz''Whampee黃皮wong-p''iThing野ye''Orange(small)桔仔,柑kut-tsai,kom,Dollar銀錢ngān-ts''inCoolieorange橙ch''angTosmoketobaccoisliterally"eatsmoke,"—anexpressiontobefoundinsomeotherlanguagesalso.Rice,asgivenabove,referstothecookedgrain.Andmayberenderedby共KUNGwhencouplingsubstantives,零LINGbeingusedbetweennumerals.Neither,however,isveryfrequentlyused.1Boilsomericedirectly即刻煲飯tsikhakpofan2Haveyouanycigarstosell?你有呂宋烟賣冇niyaulu-sung-inmaimo?3Iwanttobuyapipe我要買枝烟筒ngoiumaichiin-t''ung4Doyousmoketobacco?你食烟唔食nishikin''mshik?5Ilikebananasandcustardapples我愛蕉共番荔枝ngooitsiukungfanlai-chi6Thelycheesaregood,thewhampeesbad荔枝好黃皮唔好lai-chiho,wong-p''i''mho7Getmefiftyoranges(small)拈五十個桔仔來我nim''ngshapkokăt-tsailoingo8Boilthesausage烚個啲釀腸shăpkotiyeung-ch''eung9Takeawaythoseshrimps拈個啲蝦去nimkotihahü10Doyouliketogatherflowers?你愛摘花唔愛nioichakfa''moi?11Goandplantthosevegetables去種個啲菜hüchungkotits''oi12Thisisasilverwatch呢個時晨鏢係銀嘅nikoshi-shān-piuhaingānke13Thatisacopperbell個啲鐘銅嘅kotichungt''ungke14Iwanttobuyanironcork-screw我要買個鐵酒鑽ngoiumaikot''ittsau-tsün15Whatisthisthing?呢的係乜野nitihaimātye?16Itisanironsaucepan係鐵鑊hait''itwok17Allarehere喊嘭哈喺處ham-pang-langhaich''ü', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-043-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 43, 1, NULL, '18 What is the price of that gold watch? 响個金時晨鏢係乜價錢呢 ko ko kūn shi-shān-piu hai mât ka ts''in ni?

