The verb as given in these lists of words is to be regarded as in the infinitive mood. Thus I wish to learn, NGO CHUNG I HOK 我中意學.

Participle:—The present participle is often expressed either by the infinitive alone, or by its combination with an adverb of time. In other cases the word HAI 係 to be—is, is used, as in English, before the infinitive and adverb; e.g. "He is eating," is either he eats, K''Ü HAI YAK KĂN 佢係吃緊, or he eats at this time, K''Ü I KA YAK 佢而家吃.

The potential may is sometimes rendered by no 好.', 'Toempty整空ching''hungTolend借tse''Toemploy請,使,用ts''ing'',shai'',yung''Adog隻狗(chek)kauTofeed喂wai''Parents父母fu''mo''Tolearn學hokEverywhere處處ch''ü''-ch''ü''Adoor門munTointerpret傳話,繙譯ch''ün-wa'',fanyikAt在tsoi`Tokeep(retain)留翻laufanAfriend朋友p''angyau''Tokill打死ta''s:e''Tofind揾着wan''cheukToknow(beacquaintedwith)識shikTofinish做完tso''ünTolock鎖soh''Toheat燒熱shiuitTrue,really實shatTohurt傷sheungTheverbasgivenintheselistsofwordsistoberegardedasintheinfinitivemood.ThusIwishtolearn,NGOCHUNGIHOK我中意學.Participle:—Thepresentparticipleisoftenexpressedeitherbytheinfinitivealone,orbyitscombinationwithanadverboftime.InothercasesthewordHAI係tobe—is,isused,asinEnglish,beforetheinfinitiveandadverb;e.g."Heiseating,"iseitherheeats,K''ÜHAIYAKKĂN佢係吃緊,orheeatsatthistime,K''ÜIKAYAK佢而家吃.Thepotentialmayissometimesrenderedbyno好.', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-047-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 47, 1, NULL, 'The past participle is expressed by the adverb of time, the particle KE 嘅 sometimes following the verb, e.g., He was beaten, K''Ü PI YAN KO CHAN SHI TA TS''AN KE 佢被人个陣時打親嘅, The door was locked KO TO MUN KO CHAN SHI SOH MAI KE 响度門个陣時鎖埋嘅.

