Negatives should precede the verb, and the auxiliary the adverb, in sentences where an adverbial formation expresses the tense of the verb; e.g. He cannot write quickly佢唔寫得快 K''Ü''M SÉ TĀK FAI. He cannot do it properly佢唔做得好 K''Ü''M TSO TĀK HO.

