  ('cvh-058-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 58, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>14 No, but I can see the moon</td><td>唔得, 但係我見得個月</td><td>''m tâk; tan hai ngo kin tâk ko üt</td></tr><tr><td>15 Bring either beer or foreign wine</td><td>拈啤酒或洋酒來</td><td>nim pi tsau wak yeung tsau loi</td></tr><tr><td>16 What is that made of?</td><td>個啲係乜野做嘅</td><td>ko ti hai māt ye tso ke?</td></tr><tr><td>17 It is made of good cotton cloth</td><td>係好棉布做嘅</td><td>hai ho min-po tso ke</td></tr><tr><td>18 Make him stand up; he has stolen a fork</td><td>監佢企起身, 佢偷過一枝叉</td><td>kam k''ü ki hi shàn; k''ü t''au kwo yat chi cha</td></tr><tr><td>19 Throw it down here</td><td>擗落呢處</td><td>p''ek lok ni ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>20 Both the men have slept there</td><td>兩個人都喺个處瞓過咯</td><td>leung ko yan to hai ko ch''ü fan kwo lok</td></tr><tr><td>21 When did they swear to that?</td><td>佢哋幾時誓願响件事</td><td>k''ü-ti ki shi shai-ün ko kin sze?</td></tr><tr><td>22 Before they went away, (lit. They first swore; [they] afterwards went away)</td><td>佢哋先時誓願, 然後正咀</td><td>k''ü-ti sin-shi shai-ün; in-hau ching ch''e</td></tr><tr><td>23 Formerly they had a quarrel</td><td>佢哋舊時嗌過交</td><td>k''ü ti kau-shi ai kwo kau</td></tr><tr><td>24 There are about six of them</td><td>大約有六個處</td><td>tai yenk yau luk ko ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>25 He likes to read books</td><td>佢中意睇書</td><td>k''ü chung-i t''ai shü</td></tr><tr><td>26 Who told you so? Was it the teacher?</td><td>乜誰噉話你知: 係先生唔係</td><td>mät-shui kom wa ni chi; hai sin-shang ''m hai?</td></tr><tr><td>27 No, it was the houseboy</td><td>唔係, 係事仔</td><td>''m hai; hai sze-tsai</td></tr><tr><td>28 What did he say afterwards?</td><td>佢後來點話呢</td><td>k''ü hau loi tim wa ni?</td></tr><tr><td>29 He said both the men were bad</td><td>佢話兩個都係惡人</td><td>k''ü wa leung ko to hai ok yan</td></tr><tr><td>30 Why did he not stop them?</td><td>佢做乜唔攔住佢哋呢</td><td>k''ü tso māt ''m lan-chü k''ü-ti ni?</td></tr><tr><td>31 They had tied him up</td><td>佢哋綁嘵佢