  ('cvh-076-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 76, 1, NULL, 'The genitive or, possessive case is expressed by TI 啲 or, more commonly, by KE 嘅, though the position of a word in the sentence frequently makes its case so clear that the particle may be dispensed with; e.g. The stars of heaven, T''IN SING 天星 or T''IN KE SING 天嘅星.', 'Thegenitiveor,possessivecaseisexpressedbyTI啲or,morecommonly,byKE嘅,thoughthepositionofawordinthesentencefrequentlymakesitscasesoclearthattheparticlemaybedispensedwith;e.g.Thestarsofheaven,T''INSING天星orT''INKESING天嘅星.', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-076-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 76, 2, 'CLASSIFIERS (CONTINUED.)', '7. Chi 枝 a branch: applied to slender long round objects such as pencils pens, &c.

8. T''iu 條 a branch or twig: applied to similar objects as No. 7, and more frequently used. It is also applied to the divisions or articles of a code, and snakes, roads, whips, girdles, &c., take t''iu before them.

9. Kan 間 a crevice or interval: applied to buildings, rooms, &c. (fong kan 房間 in the rooms; ha kan 下間 below; yat nin kan 一年間 within one year.)

10. Tsoh'' 座 a seat or throne: applied to buildings, hills, cities, pagodas, seats, &c.

11. To'' 度 to pass, a limit: applied to places through, or over, which one can pass; such as doors, bridges, &c.

12. Fuk 幅 a strip of cloth: applied to maps, pictures, and similar things that are rolled up or stretched out.

A hall of meeting 一間敘 yat kau tsü'' A map 一幅地 yat fuk ti''會堂 ui'' t''ong 理圖 li'' t''o A pair of chopsticks 一對快 yat tui'' fui''子 ts'' A snake 條蛇 (t''iu) she子 tsz'' A bridge 度橋 (to'') k''iu

A house (building) 間屋（kan） uk

