  ('cvh-087-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 87, 1, 'LESSON XXX.', '<table border="1"><tr><td>An account (bill)</td><td>一條數</td><td>yat t''iu sho''</td><td>To reckon up</td><td>計起</td><td>kai'' hi''</td></tr><tr><td>A church</td><td>福音堂</td><td>fuk-yäm-t''ong</td><td>To know</td><td>知到</td><td>chi to''</td></tr><tr><td>To dislike</td><td>唔中意</td><td>''m chung-i''</td><td>To waken</td><td>呌醒</td><td>kiu'' sing''</td></tr><tr><td>To choose, select</td><td>揀擇</td><td>kán''-chak</td><td>Moreover</td><td>而且</td><td>i-ch''e''</td></tr><tr><td>To anchor</td><td>抛錨</td><td>p''au nau</td><td>The mind (heart)</td><td>心</td><td>sǎm</td></tr><tr><td>A (street) barrier</td><td>街閘</td><td>kai-chap</td><td>Troops</td><td>兵</td><td>ping</td></tr><tr><td>To stop up</td><td>.塞住</td><td>suk chü''</td><td>To level</td><td>平</td><td>p''ing</td></tr><tr><td>To follow</td><td>跟住</td><td>kan chü''</td><td>Rope</td><td>繩</td><td>shing</td></tr></table>

Adjectives usually precede, or follow, the nouns they qualify as in English; e.g., a good horse, YAT P''AT HO MA 一匹好馬; this horse is good, NI P''AT MA HO, 呢匹馬好.

Many adjectives are formed from nouns by the addition of TI 啲; e.g., better HO TI 好啲, worse, inferior, YAI-TI 昕啲. As, however, TI 啲 when following an adjective expressing form, quality, colour, or space, usually signifies the comparative degree (as in SAI-TI 細啲 smaller, TAI-TI 大啲 larger, etc.) KE 嘅 is more frequently used for such adjectives in their positive sense, though TI 啲 is sometimes retained for the sake of euphony. When two adjectival words come together, TI 啲 or KE 嘅 is generally omitted; e.g., a rich man FU-KWAI YAN 富貴人, or TS''OI-CHÜ LO 財主佬.

Beautiful 好睇 ho'' t''ai Clean 乾淨 kon-tseng'' Poor 窮 k''ung

Do. 華美 wa-mi'' Wrong 錯 ts''oh'' Old 老 lo''

Rich 財主 ts''oi-chü'' Short 短 tün'' Hot 熱 it

That is middling响個係中中嘅啫 ko''-ko` hai` chung-chung ke` che

Read that book aloud大聲讀响溥書 tai` shing tuk ko'' po` shü

I want to go to sleep我愛去瞓咯 ngo'' oi` hü` fän` lok

I dare not do it我唔敢做 ngo'' ''m kom'' tso''

I dare not presume我唔敢當 ngo'' ''m kom'' tong

Wake him up呌醒佢 kiu` sing'' k''u''

Give a little more俾啲添 pi'' ti t''im', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Anaccount(bill)</td><td>一條數</td><td>yatt''iusho''</td><td>Toreckonup</td><td>計起</td><td>kai''hi''</td></tr><tr><td>Achurch</td><td>福音堂</td><td>fuk-yäm-t''ong</td><td>Toknow</td><td>知到</td><td>chito''</td></tr><tr><td>Todislike</td><td>唔中意</td><td>''mchung-i''</td><td>Towaken</td><td>呌醒</td><td>kiu''sing''</td></tr><tr><td>Tochoose,select</td><td>揀擇</td><td>kán''-chak</td><td>Moreover</td><td>而且</td><td>i-ch''e''</td></tr><tr><td>Toanchor</td><td>抛錨</td><td>p''aunau</td><td>Themind(heart)</td><td>心</td><td>sǎm</td></tr><tr><td>A(street)barrier</td><td>街閘</td><td>kai-chap</td><td>Troops</td><td>兵</td><td>ping</td></tr><tr><td>Tostopup</td><td>.塞住</td><td>sukchü''</td><td>Tolevel</td><td>平</td><td>p''ing</td></tr><tr><td>Tofollow</td><td>跟住</td><td>kanchü''</td><td>Rope</td><td>繩</td><td>shing</td></tr></table>Adjectivesusuallyprecede,orfollow,thenounstheyqualifyasinEnglish;e.g.,agoodhorse,YATP''ATHOMA一匹好馬;thishorseisgood,NIP''ATMAHO,呢匹馬好.ManyadjectivesareformedfromnounsbytheadditionofTI啲;e.g.,betterHOTI好啲,worse,inferior,YAI-TI昕啲.As,however,TI啲whenfollowinganadjectiveexpressingform,quality,colour,orspace,usuallysignifiesthecomparativedegree(asinSAI-TI細啲smaller,TAI-TI大啲larger,etc.)KE嘅ismorefrequentlyusedforsuchadjectivesintheirpositivesense,thoughTI啲issometimesretainedforthesakeofeuphony.Whentwoadjectivalwordscometogether,TI啲orKE嘅isgenerallyomitted;e.g.,arichmanFU-KWAIYAN富貴人,orTS''OI-CHÜLO財主佬.Beautiful好睇ho''t''aiClean乾淨kon-tseng''Poor窮k''ungDo.華美wa-mi''Wrong錯ts''oh''Old老lo''Rich財主ts''oi-chü''Short短tün''Hot熱itThatismiddling响個係中中嘅啫ko''-ko`hai`chung-chungke`cheReadthatbookaloud大聲讀响溥書tai`shingtukko''po`shüIwanttogotosleep我愛去瞓咯ngo''oi`hü`fän`lokIdarenotdoit我唔敢做ngo''''mkom''tso''Idarenotpresume我唔敢當ngo''''mkom''tongWakehimup呌醒佢kiu`sing''k''u''Givealittlemore俾啲添pi''tit''im', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-088-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 88, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>To accompany friends</td><td>送朋友</td><td>sung'' p''āng-yau''</td></tr><tr><td>You are very good (kind)</td><td>你有心</td><td>ni'' yau'' sām</td></tr><tr><td>Wait for an answer</td><td>等回音</td><td>tǎng'' ni-yām</td></tr><tr><td>Speak loudly</td><td>大聲講</td><td>tai'' shing kong''</td></tr><tr><td>Wherelore?—what for?</td><td>爲乜野</td><td>wai''-màt-ye''</td></tr><tr><td>To visit a person</td><td>探人</td><td>t''am'' yan</td></tr></table>

<table border="1"><tr><td>Dining-room</td><td>大餐房</td><td>tai''-ts''an-fong</td><td>Scaffolding (bamboo)</td><td>竹棚</td><td>chuk-p''āng</td></tr><tr><td>Bath-room</td><td>洗身房</td><td>sai''-shān-fong</td><td>Study or library</td><td>書房</td><td>shü-fong</td></tr><tr><td>Bed-room</td><td>瞓房</td><td>fün''-fong</td><td>Flower-garden</td><td>花園</td><td>fu-ün</td></tr><tr><td>Steps</td><td>階級</td><td>kai-k''äp</td><td>Drawing-room</td><td>客廳</td><td>hak-t''eng</td></tr><tr><td>Lock</td><td>把鎖</td><td>pi''-soh''</td><td>Foundation</td><td>地脚</td><td>ti''-keuk</td></tr><tr><td>Key</td><td>鎖匙</td><td>soh''-shi</td><td>Brick wall</td><td>磚牆</td><td>chün ts''enug</td></tr><tr><td>Hinges</td><td>較</td><td>kuu''</td><td>Mud wall</td><td>坭牆</td><td>nai ts''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Wall</td><td>牆</td><td>ts''eung</td><td>God (the Creator)</td><td>上帝</td><td>sheung''tai''</td></tr></table>

Considerable discussion—extending to the publication of entire volumes devoted to the subject—has arisen as to the best Chinese equivalent for the word "God." That above given is now adopted by the majority of sinologues.

All, when used substantively in the sense of a relative pronoun, is idiomatically expressed by YAT KO TO 一個都.

Both and are expressed by YAU 又——YAU 又; e.g., they are all both old and poor, YAT KO TO HAI YAU LO YAU K''UNG 一個都係又老又窮.

<table border="1"><tr><td>1 Are those steps short or long?</td><td>响啲階級係長只短呢</td><td>ko-ti kai-k''ap hai ch''enng chi tün ni?</td></tr><tr><td>2 Where did the boat anchor?</td><td>响隻船抛在邊處</td><td>ko chek shün p''au tsoi pin-ch''ü?</td></tr><tr><td>3 He went to the beautiful garden</td><td>佢去响間華美嘅花園處</td><td>k''ü hui ko kan wa-mi ke fa-ün ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>4 It was very hot yesterday; to-day it is warm</td><td>昨日好熱,今日煖啫</td><td>tsok-yat ho it; kām-yat nūn che</td></tr><tr><td>5 Why do you dislike the people?</td><td>爲乜事你唔中意人哋呢</td><td>wai-mât-sze ni ''m chung-i yan ti ni?</td></tr><tr><td>6 Tell him to reckon up the bill</td><td>呌佢計起响張單</td><td>kiu k''ü kai-hi ko cheung tan</td></tr><tr><td>7 My house has a dining-room and a bed-room</td><td>我嘅屋有間大餐房共間瞓房</td><td>ngo ke nk yan kan tai-ts''an-fong kung kan làn-fong</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Toaccompanyfriends</td><td>送朋友</td><td>sung''p''āng-yau''</td></tr><tr><td>Youareverygood(kind)</td><td>你有心</td><td>ni''yau''sām</td></tr><tr><td>Waitforananswer</td><td>等回音</td><td>tǎng''ni-yām</td></tr><tr><td>Speakloudly</td><td>大聲講</td><td>tai''shingkong''</td></tr><tr><td>Wherelore?—whatfor?</td><td>爲乜野</td><td>wai''-màt-ye''</td></tr><tr><td>Tovisitaperson</td><td>探人</td><td>t''am''yan</td></tr></table><tableborder="1"><tr><td>Dining-room</td><td>大餐房</td><td>tai''-ts''an-fong</td><td>Scaffolding(bamboo)</td><td>竹棚</td><td>chuk-p''āng</td></tr><tr><td>Bath-room</td><td>洗身房</td><td>sai''-shān-fong</td><td>Studyorlibrary</td><td>書房</td><td>shü-fong</td></tr><tr><td>Bed-room</td><td>瞓房</td><td>fün''-fong</td><td>Flower-garden</td><td>花園</td><td>fu-ün</td></tr><tr><td>Steps</td><td>階級</td><td>kai-k''äp</td><td>Drawing-room</td><td>客廳</td><td>hak-t''eng</td></tr><tr><td>Lock</td><td>把鎖</td><td>pi''-soh''</td><td>Foundation</td><td>地脚</td><td>ti''-keuk</td></tr><tr><td>Key</td><td>鎖匙</td><td>soh''-shi</td><td>Brickwall</td><td>磚牆</td><td>chünts''enug</td></tr><tr><td>Hinges</td><td>較</td><td>kuu''</td><td>Mudwall</td><td>坭牆</td><td>naits''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Wall</td><td>牆</td><td>ts''eung</td><td>God(theCreator)</td><td>上帝</td><td>sheung''tai''</td></tr></table>Considerablediscussion—extendingtothepublicationofentirevolumesdevotedtothesubject—hasarisenastothebestChineseequivalentfortheword"God."Thatabovegivenisnowadoptedbythemajorityofsinologues.All,whenusedsubstantivelyinthesenseofarelativepronoun,isidiomaticallyexpressedbyYATKOTO一個都.BothandareexpressedbyYAU又——YAU又;e.g.,theyareallbotholdandpoor,YATKOTOHAIYAULOYAUK''UNG一個都係又老又窮.<tableborder="1"><tr><td>1Arethosestepsshortorlong?</td><td>响啲階級係長只短呢</td><td>ko-tikai-k''aphaich''enngchitünni?</td></tr><tr><td>2Wheredidtheboatanchor?</td><td>响隻船抛在邊處</td><td>kochekshünp''autsoipin-ch''ü?</td></tr><tr><td>3Hewenttothebeautifulgarden</td><td>佢去响間華美嘅花園處</td><td>k''ühuikokanwa-mikefa-ünch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>4Itwasveryhotyesterday;to-dayitiswarm</td><td>昨日好熱,今日煖啫</td><td>tsok-yathoit;kām-yatnūnche</td></tr><tr><td>5Whydoyoudislikethepeople?</td><td>爲乜事你唔中意人哋呢</td><td>wai-mât-szeni''mchung-iyantini?</td></tr><tr><td>6Tellhimtoreckonupthebill</td><td>呌佢計起响張單</td><td>kiuk''ükai-hikocheungtan</td></tr><tr><td>7Myhousehasadining-roomandabed-room</td><td>我嘅屋有間大餐房共間瞓房</td><td>ngokenkyankantai-ts''an-fongkungkanlàn-fong</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-089-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 89, 1, NULL, '8 Make him always keep the呌佢時時整乾淨個 kiu k''ü shi-shi ching kon-tseng bath-room clean 洗身房 ko sai-shān-fong

9 Carry those things into my 抬响啲野入去我嘅 t''oi ko-ti ye yap hü ngo ke shü-study 書房 fong

10 The foundation is not level 响啲地脚唔係平嘅 ko-ti ti-keuk ''m hai p''ing ke

11 He does his work wrongly 佢做錯佢嘅工夫咯 k''ü tso ts''oh k''ü ke kung-fu lok

12 She is old and poor 佢又老又窮 k''ü yau lo yau k''ung

13 Does he worship God at the 佢去福音堂拜上帝 k''ü hü fuk-yäm-t''ong pai sheung-Church? 唔拜呢 tai ''m pai ni?

14 There is a barrier at that place 個處有度街閘. ko-ch''ü yau to kai-chap

15 Get some rope; there is no 揾啲繩嚟; 响處冇 wan ti shing lai; ko-ch''ü mo lock there 鎖 soh

16 Tell the coolie to follow the 話個管店知跟住响 wa ko kun-tim chi kan-chü ko-troops 啲兵 ti ping

17 His heart is bad, but he fears 佢嘅心唔好,但係 k''ü ke sàm ''m ho, tan hai k''ü

me 佢怕我 p''a ngo

18 There is a scaffolding by the 响幅磚牆邊有個竹 ko-fuk chün ts''eung pin yau ko side of the brick wall 棚 chuk-p''āng

19 It is not a brick wall, it is a 响幅唔係磚牆,係 ko fuk ''m hai chün-ts''eung, hai mud wall 坭牆啫 nai-ts''eung che

20 Get the key for this lock 揾呢把鎖嘅鎖匙嚟 wan ni pa-soh ke soh-shi lai

21 Why do you want to stop up 爲乜野你要塞住响 wai-mät-ye ni iu sak chü ko to the door? 度門口 mun-hau

22 It has no hinges, and besides, 佢冇較嘅,而且又 k''ü mo kan ke, i-ch''e yau lan it''s broken爛嘵咯 hiu lok

23 Choose the good ones quickly 快快揀啲好嘅 fai-fai kān ti ho ke

24 Why should I do it quickly? 爲乜我要咁快做啫 wai-mät ngo iu kom fai tso che

25 Because I want to pay a visit 因爲我要去探一個 yan-wai ngo iu hü t''am yat ko to a person 人 yan

26 Tell the boy to read it呌個細紋仔大聲 kiu ko sai-man-tsai tai shing aloud 讀 tuk

