To stir up 攪起 kau hi To go home 去歸 hui kwai', 'Tobeseatedin坐倒tso''to''Nothing冇乜野mo''-mat-ye''Toseizeupon拉住laichü''Tocarefor(like)料理liu''li''Tosleepon瞓倒fän''to''Tohaverather寧愿ningün''Tothinkon想起seung''hi''Totieaknot打結ta''kitTohangup掛起kwa''hiWages人工yan-kungTostirup攪起kauhiTogohome去歸huikwai', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-095-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 95, 1, NULL, 'The ordinary comparison of adjectives in the Canton vernacular is very simple, the word KANG 更 for the comparative, and CHI 至, TING 頂, KIK 極, or TAI YAT 第一 for the superlative, being prefixed to the word; e.g. good HO 好, better KANG HO 更好, best CHI HO 至好. (See Lesson XXX, p. 73, upon forming the comparative by TI 啲.)

Another way of forming the comparative is to use kwo after the adjective; e.g. He is better than I, K''ü HAI HO KWO NGO 佢係好過我；This is better than that, NI-KO HO KWO Ko-ko 呢個好過响個.

The comparative is also formed by placing kwo ü 過於 after the adjective, e.g. Older than I, TAI KWO Ü NGO 大過於我.

When two comparatives occur together, the word üT 越 is placed before each; e.g. The slower the better, üT MAN üT HO 越慢越好.

<table border="1"><tr><td>Deceitful</td><td>奸詐嘅</td><td>kan-cha&#x27;ke&#x27;</td><td>Cold</td><td>凍(or)</td><td>冷tung&#x27;(or) lang&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh (as meat)</td><td>新鮮</td><td>sän-sin</td><td>Empty</td><td>空</td><td>hung</td></tr><tr><td>Faithful</td><td>忠直</td><td>chung-chik</td><td>Cool</td><td>凉</td><td>leung</td></tr><tr><td>Carefully</td><td>予細</td><td>tze&#x27;-sai&#x27;</td><td>Dry</td><td>乾</td><td>kon</td></tr><tr><td>Upright</td><td>正直</td><td>ching&#x27;-chik</td><td>Salted</td><td>鹹</td><td>ham</td></tr><tr><td>Fine (not coarse)</td><td>幼</td><td>yau&#x27;</td><td>Easy</td><td>易</td><td>i&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh (water)</td><td>淡</td><td>tam&#x27;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>

<table><tr><td>To turn inside out</td><td>翻轉裡便出嚟</td><td>fan-chun&#x27; li&#x27;-pin&#x27; ch&#x27;ut lai</td></tr><tr><td>,, upside down -</td><td>翻轉底上嚟</td><td>fan-chün&#x27; tai&#x27; sheung&#x27; lai</td></tr><tr><td>Dont be in such a hurry</td><td>唔使咁快呭</td><td>&#x27;m shai&#x27; kom&#x27; fai&#x27; chi&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>I don&#x27;t believe you</td><td>我唔信你</td><td>ngo&#x27; &#x27;m sun&#x27; ni&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Stay here</td><td>在呢處等</td><td>tsoi&#x27; ni ch&#x27;ü&#x27;tang&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>It is useless</td><td>係冇用嘅</td><td>hai&#x27; mo&#x27;-yung&#x27; ke&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Come directly</td><td>就嚟咯</td><td>tsau&#x27; lai lok</td></tr><tr><td>There is but little difference</td><td>爭有限</td><td>chang yau&#x27; han&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>He has gone home</td><td>佢去歸</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27; hü&#x27; kwai</td></tr><tr><td>Not a bit of it</td><td>并無有</td><td>ping&#x27; mo yau&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Empty it -</td><td>搬空佢</td><td>pun hung k&#x27;u&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Mix it together</td><td>攪埋佢</td><td>kau&#x27; mai k&#x27;u&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Get out of the way</td><td>行開</td><td>hang-hoi</td></tr></table>', 'TheordinarycomparisonofadjectivesintheCantonvernacularisverysimple,thewordKANG更forthecomparative,andCHI至,TING頂,KIK極,orTAIYAT第一forthesuperlative,beingprefixedtotheword;e.g.goodHO好,betterKANGHO更好,bestCHIHO至好.(SeeLessonXXX,p.73,uponformingthecomparativebyTI啲.)Anotherwayofformingthecomparativeistousekwoaftertheadjective;e.g.HeisbetterthanI,K''üHAIHOKWONGO佢係好過我；Thisisbetterthanthat,NI-KOHOKWOKo-ko呢個好過响個.Thecomparativeisalsoformedbyplacingkwoü過於aftertheadjective,e.g.OlderthanI,TAIKWOÜNGO大過於我.Whentwocomparativesoccurtogether,thewordüT越isplacedbeforeeach;e.g.Theslowerthebetter,üTMANüTHO越慢越好.<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Deceitful</td><td>奸詐嘅</td><td>kan-cha&#x27;ke&#x27;</td><td>Cold</td><td>凍(or)</td><td>冷tung&#x27;(or)lang&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh(asmeat)</td><td>新鮮</td><td>sän-sin</td><td>Empty</td><td>空</td><td>hung</td></tr><tr><td>Faithful</td><td>忠直</td><td>chung-chik</td><td>Cool</td><td>凉</td><td>leung</td></tr><tr><td>Carefully</td><td>予細</td><td>tze&#x27;-sai&#x27;</td><td>Dry</td><td>乾</td><td>kon</td></tr><tr><td>Upright</td><td>正直</td><td>ching&#x27;-chik</td><td>Salted</td><td>鹹</td><td>ham</td></tr><tr><td>Fine(notcoarse)</td><td>幼</td><td>yau&#x27;</td><td>Easy</td><td>易</td><td>i&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fresh(water)</td><td>淡</td><td>tam&#x27;</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><table><tr><td>Toturninsideout</td><td>翻轉裡便出嚟</td><td>fan-chun&#x27;li&#x27;-pin&#x27;ch&#x27;utlai</td></tr><tr><td>,,upsidedown-</td><td>翻轉底上嚟</td><td>fan-chün&#x27;tai&#x27;sheung&#x27;lai</td></tr><tr><td>Dontbeinsuchahurry</td><td>唔使咁快呭</td><td>&#x27;mshai&#x27;kom&#x27;fai&#x27;chi&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Idon&#x27;tbelieveyou</td><td>我唔信你</td><td>ngo&#x27;&#x27;msun&#x27;ni&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Stayhere</td><td>在呢處等</td><td>tsoi&#x27;nich&#x27;ü&#x27;tang&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Itisuseless</td><td>係冇用嘅</td><td>hai&#x27;mo&#x27;-yung&#x27;ke&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Comedirectly</td><td>就嚟咯</td><td>tsau&#x27;lailok</td></tr><tr><td>Thereisbutlittledifference</td><td>爭有限</td><td>changyau&#x27;han&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Hehasgonehome</td><td>佢去歸</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27;hü&#x27;kwai</td></tr><tr><td>Notabitofit</td><td>并無有</td><td>ping&#x27;moyau&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Emptyit-</td><td>搬空佢</td><td>punhungk&#x27;u&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Mixittogether</td><td>攪埋佢</td><td>kau&#x27;maik&#x27;u&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Getoutoftheway</td><td>行開</td><td>hang-hoi</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-096-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 96, 1, NULL, 'Blacking brush 鞋墨掃 hai-mak-so'' Starch 米漿 mai''-tseung

Blacking 鞋墨水 hai-mak-shu Birdcage 雀籠 tseuk-lung

Cooking pots 沙煲 sha-po Dust pan 拂斗 fut-tau''

Lamp wick 燈心 tǎng-sǎm Soap 番覰 fan-kan''

Lamp oil 生油 shāng-yan Frying pan 鑊 wok

Charcoal 煤炭 mui- t''an'' Firewood 柴 ch''ai

Coals 京炭 king-t''an Basket 籃 lam

Tongs 火鉗 fok-k''im

1 Charcoal is better than firewood 京炭好過煤炭 king t''an ho kwo mui-t''an

2 Are not coals better than煤炭唔係好過京炭 mui-t''an''m hai ho kwo king- charcoal?咩 t''an me?

3 To-day is colder than yesterday 今日冷過昨日 kam-yat lang kwo tsok-yat

4 This man is faithful; that呢個人忠直，响個ni-ko yan chung-chik; ko-ko yan man is deceitful人奸詐kan-cha

5 This cotton cloth is finer than 呢啲棉布幼細過响 ni-ti min-po yau sai kwo ko-ti that 啲

6 Do you like salt meat? 你中意鹹肉唔呢 ni chung-i ham-yuk ''m ni?

7 No, I don''t like it; I like fresh 唔中意; 我常常中 ''m chung-i; ngo sheung-sheung meat regularly (generally) 意新鮮肉 chung-i sān sin yuk

8 The weather is very cool 天時十分凉 t''in-shi shap-fan leung

9 Is not this month cooler than 呢個月唔係凉過先 ni-ko üt ''m hai leung kwo sin-ko last? 個月咩 üt me?

10 No; but it is a good deal 唔係, 但係天時乾 ''m hai; tan hai t''in-shi kon drier 好多 ho to

11 Is it easy or difficult to tie a 打個結易只難 ta ko kit (or lit) i chi nan ni?

knot? 呢

12 I have never thought about it 我未曾有想過 ngo mi ts''äng yan seung kwo

13 What has the cook done with 响個火頭擰啲鑊 ko-ko fo-t''au ning ko-ti wok kung the frying pan and pots? 共沙煲去嘵邊處 sha-po hü hiu pin-ch''ü?

14 He has put them in the basket 佢擠佢在個籃嚟 k''ü chai k''ü tsoi ko lam lai

15 Tell the boy to buy some 叫個事仔去買啲 kiu ko sze-tsai hü mai ti hai blacking to black my鞋墨水擦淨我 mak-shui ts''at tseng ngo boots對靴 tui hö', 'Blackingbrush鞋墨掃hai-mak-so''Starch米漿mai''-tseungBlacking鞋墨水hai-mak-shuBirdcage雀籠tseuk-lungCookingpots沙煲sha-poDustpan拂斗fut-tau''Lampwick燈心tǎng-sǎmSoap番覰fan-kan''Lampoil生油shāng-yanFryingpan鑊wokCharcoal煤炭mui-t''an''Firewood柴ch''aiCoals京炭king-t''anBasket籃lamTongs火鉗fok-k''im1Charcoalisbetterthanfirewood京炭好過煤炭kingt''anhokwomui-t''an2Arenotcoalsbetterthan煤炭唔係好過京炭mui-t''an''mhaihokwoking-charcoal?咩t''anme?3To-dayiscolderthanyesterday今日冷過昨日kam-yatlangkwotsok-yat4Thismanisfaithful;that呢個人忠直，响個ni-koyanchung-chik;ko-koyanmanisdeceitful人奸詐kan-cha5Thiscottonclothisfinerthan呢啲棉布幼細過响ni-timin-poyausaikwoko-tithat啲6Doyoulikesaltmeat?你中意鹹肉唔呢nichung-iham-yuk''mni?7No,Idon''tlikeit;Ilikefresh唔中意;我常常中''mchung-i;ngosheung-sheungmeatregularly(generally)意新鮮肉chung-isānsinyuk8Theweatherisverycool天時十分凉t''in-shishap-fanleung9Isnotthismonthcoolerthan呢個月唔係凉過先ni-koüt''mhaileungkwosin-kolast?個月咩ütme?10No;butitisagooddeal唔係,但係天時乾''mhai;tanhait''in-shikondrier好多hoto11Isiteasyordifficulttotiea打個結易只難takokit(orlit)ichinanni?knot?呢12Ihaveneverthoughtaboutit我未曾有想過ngomits''ängyanseungkwo13Whathasthecookdonewith响個火頭擰啲鑊ko-kofo-t''auningko-tiwokkungthefryingpanandpots?共沙煲去嘵邊處sha-pohühiupin-ch''ü?14Hehasputtheminthebasket佢擠佢在個籃嚟k''üchaik''ütsoikolamlai15Telltheboytobuysome叫個事仔去買啲kiukosze-tsaihümaitihaiblackingtoblackmy鞋墨水擦淨我mak-shuits''attsengngoboots對靴tuihö', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-097-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 97, 1, NULL, '16 Is the birdcage empty?响個雀籠空嘅咩 ko-ko tseuk-lung hung ke me?

17 Does he sleep on the floor?佢喺褸板瞓咩 k''ü lai lan-pan fān me?

18 He does not do so now; but 如今佢唔係噉做咯, ü-käm k''ü''m hai kom tso lok;

did last year 但舊年係啫 tan kau-nin hai che

19 The weather is very cold 天時十分冷 t''in-shi shap-fan lang

20 For me the colder the better 我就越冷越好 ngo tsau üt lang üt ho

21 What was he seated in? 佢坐住乜野呢 k''ü tso chü mât-ye ni?

22 He was seated in the carriage 佢坐在馬車嚟 k''ü tso tsoi ma-ch''e lai

23 I thought he was seated in a 我估佢坐在艇 ngo ku k''ü tso tsoi t''ing lai boat 嚟

24 Hang up that birdcage on the 掛起個雀籠在個牆 kwa hi ko tseuk-lung tsoi ko wall 上嚟 ts''eung sheung lai

25 Buy some lamp oil and wick 買啲燈心共油過 mai ti tǎng-sām kung yau kwo for me 我 ngo

26 Did he seize upon those people? 佢濜住响啲人咩 k''ü lai chü ko-ti yan me?

27 Yes; but it was no use係但唔濟事咯 hai, tan ''m tsai sze lok

28 I had rather he had not 我寧愿佢唔會噉 ngo ning-ün k''ü''m ts''üng kom done so 做喇 tso la

29 Don''t let him stir it up 咪俾佢攪起佢 mai pi k''ü kau-hi k''ü

30 Why won''t he go home? 爲乜事佢唔肯去

歸呢 wai-mät-sze k''ü''m hang hü kwai

ni?

31 He does not care to; he has 佢唔多想啫.佢冇 k''ü''m to seung che, k''ü mo yan-

no wages 人工嘅 kung ke

32 Is there anything there? 响處有野冇呢 ko-ch''ü yau ye mo ni?

33 No; there is nothing 冇,响處冇野 mo, ko-ch''ü mo ye

34 I don''t believe it; go and see 我唔信，去睇下喇 ngo''m sān, hui t''ai ha la

