  ('cvh-136-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 136, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>Salary (lit. firewood and water)</td><td>俸祿</td><td>fung''-luk</td><td>Deceit</td><td>詭譎</td><td>kwai''-kwät''</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="3">To get out of the way</td><td rowspan="3">行開</td><td rowspan="3">hang-hoi''</td><td>Wages</td><td>人工</td><td>yan-kung</td></tr><tr><td>To hurry</td><td>急</td><td>käp</td></tr><tr><td>Late</td><td>遲</td><td>ch''i</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>Salary(lit.firewoodandwater)</td><td>俸祿</td><td>fung''-luk</td><td>Deceit</td><td>詭譎</td><td>kwai''-kwät''</td></tr><tr><tdrowspan="3">Togetoutoftheway</td><tdrowspan="3">行開</td><tdrowspan="3">hang-hoi''</td><td>Wages</td><td>人工</td><td>yan-kung</td></tr><tr><td>Tohurry</td><td>急</td><td>käp</td></tr><tr><td>Late</td><td>遲</td><td>ch''i</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-136-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 136, 2, 'NUMERALS.', 'With the ordinary numerals the student is already familiar. These are however written in two other ways besides the forms already given, and those who are studying the character will find it advantageous to acquire them from a teacher. The mode here adopted is that usually found in books. The more complicated form is used in important documents to lessen the chance of fraud; and the other is a contracted form used in arithmetical computations and current accounts.

In counting from 100 to 110 the character LING 零 is introduced before the additional number; e.g., 100=YAT PAK 一百; 110=YAT PAK LING SHAP 一百零十.

The word signifying ten is often omitted after the hundred; e.g. 150 = YAT PAK ''NG 一百五；1000 = YAT TS''IN 一千；a myriad =一萬 YAT MAN.

The numerals enter into a large number of phrases in common use and in which their actual numerical signification is lost sight of. In most cases, however, this is easily traceable

IDIOMATIC USES of. One, YAT 一.

<table><tr><td>Disagreement (<i>lit.</i> not of one mind)</td><td>心不一</td><td>säm pat yat</td><td>One by one</td><td>一一</td><td>yat ya''</td></tr><tr><td>Glance at it</td><td>睇一吓</td><td>t''ai'' yat ha''</td><td>Whilst</td><td>一面</td><td>yat min''</td></tr><tr><td>The whole life</td><td>一生</td><td>yat shäng</td><td>Addicted</td><td>專一</td><td>chün yat</td></tr><tr><td>As soon as he left</td><td>一往</td><td>yat wong''</td><td>As soon as</td><td>一經</td><td>yat king</td></tr></table>

<table><tr><td>I can''t put it there</td><td>唔擠得响處</td><td>''m chui tāk ko''-ch''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>A heavy cargo -</td><td>好重嘅貨物</td><td>ho'' chung'' ke'' foh''-mät</td></tr><tr><td>There is no room</td><td>冇地方</td><td>mo'' ti''-fong</td></tr><tr><td>A head wind</td><td>頂頭風</td><td>ting'' t''au fung</td></tr><tr><td>A fair wind</td><td>順風</td><td>shun'' fung</td></tr><tr><td>A fair tide</td><td>順水</td><td>shun'' shui''</td></tr><tr><td>A head tide</td><td>逆水</td><td>yik shui''</td></tr></table>', 'Withtheordinarynumeralsthestudentisalreadyfamiliar.Thesearehoweverwrittenintwootherwaysbesidestheformsalreadygiven,andthosewhoarestudyingthecharacterwillfinditadvantageoustoacquirethemfromateacher.Themodehereadoptedisthatusuallyfoundinbooks.Themorecomplicatedformisusedinimportantdocumentstolessenthechanceoffraud;andtheotherisacontractedformusedinarithmeticalcomputationsandcurrentaccounts.Incountingfrom100to110thecharacterLING零isintroducedbeforetheadditionalnumber;e.g.,100=YATPAK一百;110=YATPAKLINGSHAP一百零十.Thewordsignifyingtenisoftenomittedafterthehundred;e.g.150=YATPAK''NG一百五；1000=YATTS''IN一千；amyriad=一萬YATMAN.Thenumeralsenterintoalargenumberofphrasesincommonuseandinwhichtheiractualnumericalsignificationislostsightof.Inmostcases,however,thisiseasilytraceableIDIOMATICUSESof.One,YAT一.<table><tr><td>Disagreement(<i>lit.</i>notofonemind)</td><td>心不一</td><td>sämpatyat</td><td>Onebyone</td><td>一一</td><td>yatya''</td></tr><tr><td>Glanceatit</td><td>睇一吓</td><td>t''ai''yatha''</td><td>Whilst</td><td>一面</td><td>yatmin''</td></tr><tr><td>Thewholelife</td><td>一生</td><td>yatshäng</td><td>Addicted</td><td>專一</td><td>chünyat</td></tr><tr><td>Assoonasheleft</td><td>一往</td><td>yatwong''</td><td>Assoonas</td><td>一經</td><td>yatking</td></tr></table><table><tr><td>Ican''tputitthere</td><td>唔擠得响處</td><td>''mchuitākko''-ch''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>Aheavycargo-</td><td>好重嘅貨物</td><td>ho''chung''ke''foh''-mät</td></tr><tr><td>Thereisnoroom</td><td>冇地方</td><td>mo''ti''-fong</td></tr><tr><td>Aheadwind</td><td>頂頭風</td><td>ting''t''aufung</td></tr><tr><td>Afairwind</td><td>順風</td><td>shun''fung</td></tr><tr><td>Afairtide</td><td>順水</td><td>shun''shui''</td></tr><tr><td>Aheadtide</td><td>逆水</td><td>yikshui''</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
