  ('cvh-149-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 149, 1, NULL, '4 I stay one third of the time 我在省三分有一咁 ngo tsoi Shăng sam fān yau yat at Canton and two thirds at 耐, 在香港三分 kom noi, tsoi Heung-kong Hongkong 有二咁耐 sam fān yau i kom noi

5 Is tomorrow new year''s day? 聽日係年初一咩 t''ing-yat hai nin ch''oh yat me?

6 No, it is the first day of the 唔係, 係閏月初一 ''m hai, hai yun üt ch''oh yat intercalary month啫 che

7 He came here about noon; and 佢上下晏晝來; 下 k''ü sheung ha an-chan loi; ha-went in the afternoon 午就去曉咯 ''ng tsau hü hiu lok

8 What o''clock was it when he 佢來時幾多點鐘 k''ü loi shi ki to tim chung came? 呢 ni?

9 It was a quarter past two 係兩點一個角 hai leung tim yat ko kok

10 There were six rows of trees in the garden 個花園有六刺樹 ko fa-ün yau luk lat shü

11 He has a very fine looking glass 佢有一個面鏡十分好嘅 k''ü yau yat ko min-keng shap-fan ho ke

12 Women wear earrings; men wear finger rings 女人帶耳環，男人帶戒指 nü-yan tai i-wan; nam-yan tai kai-chi

13 Pat the money in your purse 擠個啲銀在你嘅腰屏袋 chai ko-ti ngan tsoi ni ke iu-p''ing-toi

14 The needle-woman makes shirts 個補衫婆做汗衫 ko po-sham-p''oh tso hon-sham

15 Do you require spectacles? 你要帶眼鏡咩 ni in tai ngan-keng me?

16 Do Foreigners and Chinese take snuff? 外國人共唐人都食鼻烟咩 ngoi-kwok yan kung T''ong-yan to shik pi-in me?

17 Yes, Foreigners use snuff boxes; Chinese use snuff bottles 係，外國人用鼻烟盒，唐人用鼻烟壺 hai; ngoi-kwok yan yung pi-in-hop; T''ong-yan yung pi-in-u

18 Women do not wear neckties 女人唔攬頸帶嘅 nü-yan ''m lam keng-tai ke

