  ('cvh-162-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 162, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>25</td><td>I prefer duck''s eggs if they are boiled</td><td>若係烚嘅我中意鴨蛋</td><td>yeuk hai shap ke ngo chung-i ap-tan</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>Did you ever eat salted hen''s eggs?</td><td>你有食鹹鷄蛋冇呢</td><td>ni yau shik ham kai-tan mo ni?</td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>What are salted eggs? I never heard of them</td><td>鹹蛋係乜野呢, 我未曾聞過</td><td>ham tan hai mät-ye ni? ngo mi ts''ang män kwo</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>All Chinese eat salted eggs</td><td>喊嘭哈唐人都食鹹蛋嘅</td><td>ham-pang-lan T''ong-yan to shik ham-tan ke</td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>I have not seen them anywhere</td><td>我處處都冇見過佢哋</td><td>ngo ch''ü-ch''ü to mo kin kwo k''ü-ti</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Buy me a catty of beef steaks</td><td>買一斤牛肉鈀過我</td><td>mai yat kān ngau-yuk-p''a kwo ngo</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>Had I not better buy one pound?</td><td>我唔係買一磅咩</td><td>ngo ''m hai mai yat pong me?</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>Beche-de mer is sold by the picul</td><td>海參係成担賣嘅</td><td>hoi-shām hai shing tam mai ke</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>How many ounces make a catty?</td><td>幾多兩爲一斤呢</td><td>ki to leung wai yat kān ni?</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>Sixteen Chinese ounces make one catty</td><td>唐人十六兩爲一斤</td><td>T''ong-yan shap-luk leung wai yat kān</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>How many catties make a picul?</td><td>幾多斤爲一担呢</td><td>ki to kān wai yat tam ni?</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>A picul contains one hundred catties</td><td>一担即係一百斤</td><td>yat tam tsik hai yat pak kān</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>A shik, then, is more than a picul?</td><td>一石多過一担咩</td><td>yat shek to kwo yat tam me?</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>A shik is one hundred and twenty catties</td><td>一石即係一百零二十斤</td><td>yat shek tsik hai yat pak ling i-shap kān</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>There is then but little difference between the two?</td><td>兩樣都係唔同嘅咩</td><td>leung yeung to hai ''m t''ung ke me?</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>There is a difference of twenty catties</td><td>爭二十斤唔同</td><td>chǎng i-shap kān ''m t''ung</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>25</td><td>Ipreferduck''seggsiftheyareboiled</td><td>若係烚嘅我中意鴨蛋</td><td>yeukhaishapkengochung-iap-tan</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>Didyouevereatsaltedhen''seggs?</td><td>你有食鹹鷄蛋冇呢</td><td>niyaushikhamkai-tanmoni?</td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>Whataresaltedeggs?Ineverheardofthem</td><td>鹹蛋係乜野呢,我未曾聞過</td><td>hamtanhaimät-yeni?ngomits''angmänkwo</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>AllChineseeatsaltedeggs</td><td>喊嘭哈唐人都食鹹蛋嘅</td><td>ham-pang-lanT''ong-yantoshikham-tanke</td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>Ihavenotseenthemanywhere</td><td>我處處都冇見過佢哋</td><td>ngoch''ü-ch''ütomokinkwok''ü-ti</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Buymeacattyofbeefsteaks</td><td>買一斤牛肉鈀過我</td><td>maiyatkānngau-yuk-p''akwongo</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>HadInotbetterbuyonepound?</td><td>我唔係買一磅咩</td><td>ngo''mhaimaiyatpongme?</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>Beche-demerissoldbythepicul</td><td>海參係成担賣嘅</td><td>hoi-shāmhaishingtammaike</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>Howmanyouncesmakeacatty?</td><td>幾多兩爲一斤呢</td><td>kitoleungwaiyatkānni?</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>SixteenChineseouncesmakeonecatty</td><td>唐人十六兩爲一斤</td><td>T''ong-yanshap-lukleungwaiyatkān</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>Howmanycattiesmakeapicul?</td><td>幾多斤爲一担呢</td><td>kitokānwaiyattamni?</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>Apiculcontainsonehundredcatties</td><td>一担即係一百斤</td><td>yattamtsikhaiyatpakkān</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>Ashik,then,ismorethanapicul?</td><td>一石多過一担咩</td><td>yatshektokwoyattamme?</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>Ashikisonehundredandtwentycatties</td><td>一石即係一百零二十斤</td><td>yatshektsikhaiyatpaklingi-shapkān</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>Thereisthenbutlittledifferencebetweenthetwo?</td><td>兩樣都係唔同嘅咩</td><td>leungyeungtohai''mt''ungkeme?</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>Thereisadifferenceoftwentycatties</td><td>爭二十斤唔同</td><td>chǎngi-shapkān''mt''ung</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-163-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 163, 1, 'ADVERBS AND ADVERBIAL EXPRESSIONS OF PRESENT TIME.', '<table><tr><td>In the morning</td><td>朝頭早</td><td>chiu-t''au-tso''</td><td>To this day</td><td>至到今日</td><td>chi'' to'' kǎm-yat</td></tr><tr><td>At night</td><td>夜晚黑</td><td>ye''-man''-hak</td><td>Day-time</td><td>日頭</td><td>yat-t''au</td></tr><tr><td>This morning</td><td>今朝</td><td>kàm-chiu</td><td>By day</td><td>日間</td><td>yat-kan</td></tr><tr><td>This evening</td><td>今晚</td><td>kàm-man''</td><td>Now, at present</td><td>如今</td><td>ü-kǎm</td></tr><tr><td>To-night</td><td>今夜</td><td>kǎm-ye''</td><td>Now-a-days</td><td>近來</td><td>kān-loi</td></tr><tr><td>Mid-night</td><td>半夜</td><td>pun-ye''</td><td>This time</td><td>呢陳</td><td>ni-chǎn''</td></tr><tr><td>By night</td><td>夜間</td><td>ye''-kan</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>

A processsion 出遊 ch''ut-yau

A tube 筒 t''ung

70. Pan'' 板 a board, slab, is applied to processions, shallow vessels of wood, &c.

71. Chü 株 a trunk,} & Kǎn 根 a root,} are , trees.

72. *Kun''* 管 a reed, is , tubes (chiefly those of bamboo)

A thorough acquaintance with the auxiliary parts of speech, such as adverbs, prepositions, etc., is of the highest importance to the student who would learn to accurately express those shades of meaning implied in English by the tenses of verbs. Copious vocabularies of such words are therefore given in these lessons.

MEASURES OF LENGTH.

<table><tr><td>1</td><td>Nap</td><td>粒</td><td>or grain</td><td>=</td><td>1</td><td>Făn</td><td>分</td><td>or division</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Făn</td><td>分</td><td></td><td>=</td><td>1</td><td>Ts''ün''</td><td>寸</td><td>or inch</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Ts''ün''</td><td>寸</td><td></td><td>=</td><td>1</td><td>Ch''ek</td><td>尺</td><td>or foot</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Ch''ek</td><td>尺</td><td></td><td>=</td><td>1</td><td>Cheung''</td><td>丈</td><td>or rod</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Cheung''</td><td>丈</td><td></td><td>=</td><td>1</td><td>Yan''</td><td>仞</td><td>of eight cubits</td></tr></table>

