  ('cvh-179-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 179, 2, 'LESSON LIV.', 'ADVERBS AND ADVERBIAL EXPRESSIONS OF NUMBER AND ORDER.

The word ch''o 初 to begin, commence, enters into certain combinations expressing "first" and is specially used with the first ten numbers of a series, such as the days of the month etc.; e.g., ch''o YAT 初一 the first, ch''o I 初二 the second; ch''o KIN 初見 the first interview.

UN 元 original, is also used for the first day, month, year, &c.: UN-TAN 元旦 new year''s day.

Every other day {每第二日 mui'' tai'' i'' yat Firstly 一來 yat loi

Secondly 二來 i'' loi', 'ADVERBSANDADVERBIALEXPRESSIONSOFNUMBERANDORDER.Thewordch''o初tobegin,commence,entersintocertaincombinationsexpressing"first"andisspeciallyusedwiththefirsttennumbersofaseries,suchasthedaysofthemonthetc.;e.g.,ch''oYAT初一thefirst,ch''oI初二thesecond;ch''oKIN初見thefirstinterview.UN元original,isalsousedforthefirstday,month,year,&c.:UN-TAN元旦newyear''sday.Everyotherday{每第二日mui''tai''i''yatFirstly一來yatloiSecondly二來i''loi', 'verified'),
