  ('cvh-193-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 193, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>To mark goods</td><td>落暗號</td><td>lok om&#x27;-ho&#x27;</td><td>To make verses</td><td>吟詩</td><td>yǎm shi</td></tr><tr><td>Revolver (pistol)</td><td>六口連</td><td>luk-hau&#x27;-lin</td><td>Politeness</td><td>禮貌</td><td>lai&#x27;-mau&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Muslin</td><td>袈裟布</td><td>ka-sha-po&#x27;</td><td>Do.(rules of)</td><td>禮數</td><td>lai&#x27;-sho&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>A muster(pattern)</td><td>樣子</td><td>yeung&#x27;-tsz&#x27;</td><td>Mud fort</td><td>坭城</td><td>nai-shing</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>辦</td><td>pan&#x27;</td><td>Ocean</td><td>洋海</td><td>yeung-hoi&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Oar</td><td>槳</td><td>tseung&#x27;</td><td>Mouse</td><td>石鼠</td><td>shek-shu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>To pull the oars</td><td>掉槳</td><td>chau&#x27; tseung&#x27;</td><td>Bat</td><td>飛鼠</td><td>fi-shu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fowling piece</td><td>鳥鎗</td><td>niu&#x27;-ts&#x27;eung</td><td>Postage</td><td>信資</td><td>sun&#x27;-tsz</td></tr><tr><td>Marriage</td><td>嫁娶</td><td>ka&#x27; ts&#x27;ü&#x27;</td><td>Monkey</td><td>馬騮</td><td>ma&#x27;-lau</td></tr><tr><td>Trade</td><td>生意</td><td>shǎng-i&#x27;</td><td>Do.(a slang term)</td><td>亞三</td><td>a&#x27;-sam</td></tr><tr><td>Pistol</td><td>手鎗</td><td>shau&#x27;-ts&#x27;eung</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>An ignoramus</td><td>山佬</td><td>shan-lo&#x27;</td><td>Mosquito</td><td>蚊</td><td>mǎn</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>山毒</td><td>shan-tuk</td><td>Poetry</td><td>詩</td><td>shi</td></tr><tr><td>Placard</td><td>標紅</td><td>piu-hung</td><td>Poison</td><td>毒</td><td>tuk</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>街招</td><td>kai-chiu</td><td>Net</td><td>網</td><td>mong&#x27;</td></tr></table>

1 I hear that there is a monkey 我聞得响處有隻馬 ngo măn tăk ko-ch''ü yau chek at that place 騮 ma-lau

2 About how much will it cost 大約要幾多錢正養 tai yeuk iu ki to ts''in ching yeung to feed it? 得佢呢 täk k''ü ni?

3 Will you go to see it? 你去睇响啲咩 ni hü t''ai ko-ti me?

4 That will be according to the 照依天時嚟奏 chiu-i t''in-shi lai ts''au weather

5 Do you know whether you 你知到你在屋裡嚟 ni chi to ni tsoi uk li lai ''m a? will be at home? 唔呀

6 I shall be for the present; 現時在, 而且我失 in-shi tsoi; i-ch''e ngo shat ko-

besides, I cannot miss 响啲的樂音 ti ngok-yǎm ''m

the music 唔好 ho

7 I want to write to him because 我要寫信過佢因爲 ngo iu se sun kwo k''ü yan-wai of the mistake 响啲錯處 ko-ti ts''oh ch''ü

8 You must not let the mud get 你唔好俾啲泥整親 ni ''m ho pi ti nai ching ts''ăn ni on your clothes 你嘅衫 ke sham

9 Send a muster of these goods 寄呢啲貨辦去我嘅 ki ni-ti foh-pan hü ngo ke to my house 屋嚟 uk lai', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Tomarkgoods</td><td>落暗號</td><td>lokom&#x27;-ho&#x27;</td><td>Tomakeverses</td><td>吟詩</td><td>yǎmshi</td></tr><tr><td>Revolver(pistol)</td><td>六口連</td><td>luk-hau&#x27;-lin</td><td>Politeness</td><td>禮貌</td><td>lai&#x27;-mau&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Muslin</td><td>袈裟布</td><td>ka-sha-po&#x27;</td><td>Do.(rulesof)</td><td>禮數</td><td>lai&#x27;-sho&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Amuster(pattern)</td><td>樣子</td><td>yeung&#x27;-tsz&#x27;</td><td>Mudfort</td><td>坭城</td><td>nai-shing</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>辦</td><td>pan&#x27;</td><td>Ocean</td><td>洋海</td><td>yeung-hoi&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Oar</td><td>槳</td><td>tseung&#x27;</td><td>Mouse</td><td>石鼠</td><td>shek-shu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Topulltheoars</td><td>掉槳</td><td>chau&#x27;tseung&#x27;</td><td>Bat</td><td>飛鼠</td><td>fi-shu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Fowlingpiece</td><td>鳥鎗</td><td>niu&#x27;-ts&#x27;eung</td><td>Postage</td><td>信資</td><td>sun&#x27;-tsz</td></tr><tr><td>Marriage</td><td>嫁娶</td><td>ka&#x27;ts&#x27;ü&#x27;</td><td>Monkey</td><td>馬騮</td><td>ma&#x27;-lau</td></tr><tr><td>Trade</td><td>生意</td><td>shǎng-i&#x27;</td><td>Do.(aslangterm)</td><td>亞三</td><td>a&#x27;-sam</td></tr><tr><td>Pistol</td><td>手鎗</td><td>shau&#x27;-ts&#x27;eung</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Anignoramus</td><td>山佬</td><td>shan-lo&#x27;</td><td>Mosquito</td><td>蚊</td><td>mǎn</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>山毒</td><td>shan-tuk</td><td>Poetry</td><td>詩</td><td>shi</td></tr><tr><td>Placard</td><td>標紅</td><td>piu-hung</td><td>Poison</td><td>毒</td><td>tuk</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>街招</td><td>kai-chiu</td><td>Net</td><td>網</td><td>mong&#x27;</td></tr></table>1Ihearthatthereisamonkey我聞得响處有隻馬ngomăntăkko-ch''üyauchekatthatplace騮ma-lau2Abouthowmuchwillitcost大約要幾多錢正養taiyeukiukitots''inchingyeungtofeedit?得佢呢täkk''üni?3Willyougotoseeit?你去睇响啲咩nihüt''aiko-time?4Thatwillbeaccordingtothe照依天時嚟奏chiu-it''in-shilaits''auweather5Doyouknowwhetheryou你知到你在屋裡嚟nichitonitsoiuklilai''ma?willbeathome?唔呀6Ishallbeforthepresent;現時在,而且我失in-shitsoi;i-ch''engoshatko-besides,Icannotmiss响啲的樂音tingok-yǎm''mthemusic唔好ho7Iwanttowritetohimbecause我要寫信過佢因爲ngoiusesunkwok''üyan-waiofthemistake响啲錯處ko-tits''ohch''ü8Youmustnotletthemudget你唔好俾啲泥整親ni''mhopitinaichingts''ănnionyourclothes你嘅衫kesham9Sendamusterofthesegoods寄呢啲貨辦去我嘅kini-tifoh-panhüngoketomyhouse屋嚟uklai', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-194-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 194, 1, NULL, '10 The moon is behind the個月在响個山後便ko üt tsoi ko-ko shan hau-pin mountaius嚟lai

11 What is that writing below the 响個暗號下底寫乜 ko-ko om-ho ha-tai se măt-ye tsz private mark? 野字嚟呢 lai ni?

12 That remark might have been 或者响句係冇乜意 wak-che ko kü hai mo măt i-sz without meaning思嘅 ke

13 The Chinese do a good deal of money-changing 唐人好多做找換嘅生意 T''ong-yan ho to tso chau-un ke shang-i

14 The moon is always bright 呢陣時個月常時係 ni-chan shi ko üt sheung-shi hai just now 好光 ho kwong

15 The mosquitos are very trouble-個啲蚊係十分煩擾 ko-ti mān hai shap-fān fan-iu;

some; I must use a net 我要用個網 ngo iu yung ko mong

16 England is situated beyond英國係在洋海外 Ying-kwok hai tsoi yeung hoi the ocean ngoi

17 Why do they stick up placards 佢哋爲乜野貼街招 k''ü-ti wai-mät-ye t''ip kai-chiu about it? 呢 ni?

18 Because they come from the 因爲佢哋由海上來 yan-wai k''ü-ti yau hoi sheung sea 嘅 loi ke

19 While I was smoking my pipe, 我食僅烟時見一隻 ngo shik kau in shi kin yat chek

I saw a mouse 石鼠 shek-shü

20 There is not sufficient room to 呢處唔够地方坐 ni-ch''ü ''m kau ti-fong tso sit down here

21 Can you pull two oars at one 你一齊掉得兩枝槳 ni yat ts''ai chau täk leung chi time? 唔呢 tseung ''m ni?

22 I did so when I was working 我先日在艇打工時 ngo sin-yat tsoi t''ing ta kung shi in a boat 有用 yau yung

23 They use a great deal of paste 佢哋用好多漿糊貼 k''ü-ti yung ho to tseung-n t''ip to stick up the placards 响啲街招 ko-ti kai-chiu

24 Do you ever smoke opium? 你有食過鴉片烟冇 ni yau shik kwo a-p''in-in mo ni?

It is very bad 呢; 係十分唔好 hai shap-fan ''m ho

25 I used to have a revolver; you 我先時有枝六口連, ngo sin-shi yau chi luk-hau-lin;

had only a common 你有枝平常手 ni yau chip p''ing-sheung shau-

pistol 鎗啫 ts''eung che', '10Themoonisbehindthe個月在响個山後便koüttsoiko-koshanhau-pinmountaius嚟lai11Whatisthatwritingbelowthe响個暗號下底寫乜ko-koom-hoha-taisemăt-yetszprivatemark?野字嚟呢laini?12Thatremarkmighthavebeen或者响句係冇乜意wak-chekokühaimomăti-szwithoutmeaning思嘅ke13TheChinesedoagooddealofmoney-changing唐人好多做找換嘅生意T''ong-yanhototsochau-unkeshang-i14Themoonisalwaysbright呢陣時個月常時係ni-chanshikoütsheung-shihaijustnow好光hokwong15Themosquitosareverytrouble-個啲蚊係十分煩擾ko-timānhaishap-fānfan-iu;some;Imustuseanet我要用個網ngoiuyungkomong16Englandissituatedbeyond英國係在洋海外Ying-kwokhaitsoiyeunghoitheoceanngoi17Whydotheystickupplacards佢哋爲乜野貼街招k''ü-tiwai-mät-yet''ipkai-chiuaboutit?呢ni?18Becausetheycomefromthe因爲佢哋由海上來yan-waik''ü-tiyauhoisheungsea嘅loike19WhileIwassmokingmypipe,我食僅烟時見一隻ngoshikkauinshikinyatchekIsawamouse石鼠shek-shü20Thereisnotsufficientroomto呢處唔够地方坐ni-ch''ü''mkauti-fongtsositdownhere21Canyoupulltwooarsatone你一齊掉得兩枝槳niyatts''aichautäkleungchitime?唔呢tseung''mni?22IdidsowhenIwasworking我先日在艇打工時ngosin-yattsoit''ingtakungshiinaboat有用yauyung23Theyuseagreatdealofpaste佢哋用好多漿糊貼k''ü-tiyunghototseung-nt''iptostickuptheplacards响啲街招ko-tikai-chiu24Doyoueversmokeopium?你有食過鴉片烟冇niyaushikkwoa-p''in-inmoni?Itisverybad呢;係十分唔好haishap-fan''mho25Iusedtohavearevolver;you我先時有枝六口連,ngosin-shiyauchiluk-hau-lin;hadonlyacommon你有枝平常手niyauchipp''ing-sheungshau-pistol鎗啫ts''eungche', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-195-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 195, 1, NULL, '26 I was very fond of play when 我細蚊仔時好反斗 ngo sai-măn-tsai shi ho fan-tau

I was a boy 嘅 ko

27 Do you like poetry? I some- 你中意詩唔呢, 我 ni chung-i shi ''m ni? ngo yau-shi times make verses 有時吟詩 yǎm shi

28 No; I do not, though many 唔中意,唔噲,雖係 ''m chung-i; ''m ui, sui hai ho people do 好多人噲 to yau ui

29 Have you ever seen a man 你有見過人服毒藥 ni yau kin kwo yan fuk tuk-yeuk take poison? 冇呢 mo ni?

30 The Chinese are very polite 唐人大家十分好禮 T''ong-yan tai-ka shap-fan ho lai-

(to each other) 數 sho

31 Have you received your port 你有接到放行紙冇 ni yau tsip to fong-hang-chi mo clearance yet? 呢 ni?

32 No; they would not give it me 冇, 佢哋唔肯俾我 mo, k''ü-ti ''m hang pi ngo

33 What is the postage of a letter 寄封信去英國要幾 ki fung sun hü Ying-kwok iu ki to England? 多信資呢 to sun-tsze ni?

34 I think it is about thirty 我估要三十個先士, ngo ku iu sam-shap-ko sin-sz, wak

cents, perhaps it may 或者重要多啲 che chung iu to ti to

be more 都唔定 ''m ting

35 Has there been any fire lately 香港近日有火燭冇 Heung-kong kán-yat yau foh-chuk in Hong-kong ? 呢 mo ni?

36 There was a small one last昨夜有小小火燭 tsok-ye yau siu-siu foh-chuk night啫 che

37 Do you use warm water for 如今你重用煖水洗 ü-käm ni chung yung nün-shui sai washing your face now? 面唔呢 min ''m ni？

