  ('cvh-209-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 209, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>33</td><td>I am anxious to buy some blue silk gauze</td><td>我十分中意買啲藍紗</td><td>ngo shap-fan chung-i mai ti lam-sha</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>What is the difference between gauze and crape?</td><td>紗共縐紗有乜分別呢</td><td>sha kung tsau-sha yau măt fän-pit ni?</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>One is much thicker and stronger than the other</td><td>一樣厚嘅及主固過响樣</td><td>yat yung hau ke kap chü-ku kwo ko yeung</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>The nett weight of that floss silk is but trifling</td><td>個啲絲絨淨重係爭有限啫</td><td>ko-ti sze-yung tsing ch''ung hai chang yau hau che</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>What means have you of weighing it</td><td>你有乜野方法秤佢呢</td><td>ni yau măt-ye fong-fat ch''ing k''ü ni?</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>We use scales and weights made of copper</td><td>我哋用秤共銅做嘅碼子</td><td>ngo-ti yung ch''ing, kung t''ung tso ke ma-tsz</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>I can''t bear this illness any longer</td><td>我唔抵得住噉嘅病添咯</td><td>ngo ''m tai tăk chü kom ke peng t''im lok</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>There are a great many illnesses to be met with in the world</td><td>世間有好多病症碰着嘅</td><td>shai-kan yau ho to peng-ching p''ung cheuk ke</td></tr></table>

