  ('rcc-048-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 48, 1, NULL, 'He works in the fields.

Your father works all day long, and he gets money and brings it home to mother. He says to your mother, ''Buy some bread with this money, and give some of it to the children.''— ''Peep of Day,'' p. 11.

佢日日打工贃翻嚟嘅。

你父親成日打工、贃倒錢拈翻歸、俾過你老母、佢對你老母話、拈呢啲錢買食物養仔女啦。', 'Heworksinthefields.Yourfatherworksalldaylong,andhegetsmoneyandbringsithometomother.Hesaystoyourmother,''Buysomebreadwiththismoney,andgivesomeofittothechildren.''—''PeepofDay,''p.11.佢日日打工贃翻嚟嘅。你父親成日打工、贃倒錢拈翻歸、俾過你老母、佢對你老母話、拈呢啲錢買食物養仔女啦。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-048-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 48, 2, 'LESSON, III.', 'In the spring he takes his scythe to mow the grass, and as he mows be bends his back till it aches. In harvest time he takes his sickle and reaps, while the hot sun beats upon his poor head.

In the cold weather he follows the plough, while the cold rain and sleet beat upon his face.

Why does he bear all this?

年頭之時,要出力爬田掘地,有時去撒穀,有時去插禾,喺田處,個啲熱頭晒得好關係,晒到個頭壳都痢呀。

That you may have plenty of food and be fat and rosy.—''Peep of Day,'' p. 12.

到割禾個時，又要出好到手力呀。佢做嘅工夫，唔論冷熱，唔論好天落雨，都要去做。

你估佢爲乜做咁多工夫，都唔怕辛苦呢。

佢都係想你唔抵肚餓又想養得你肥肥壯壯啫。', 'Inthespringhetakeshisscythetomowthegrass,andashemowsbebendshisbacktillitaches.Inharvesttimehetakeshissickleandreaps,whilethehotsunbeatsuponhispoorhead.Inthecoldweatherhefollowstheplough,whilethecoldrainandsleetbeatuponhisface.Whydoeshebearallthis?年頭之時,要出力爬田掘地,有時去撒穀,有時去插禾,喺田處,個啲熱頭晒得好關係,晒到個頭壳都痢呀。Thatyoumayhaveplentyoffoodandbefatandrosy.—''PeepofDay,''p.12.到割禾個時，又要出好到手力呀。佢做嘅工夫，唔論冷熱，唔論好天落雨，都要去做。你估佢爲乜做咁多工夫，都唔怕辛苦呢。佢都係想你唔抵肚餓又想養得你肥肥壯壯啫。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-049-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 49, 1, NULL, '⁵K''öü yat₂-yat₂ ''tá-kung chán² fán lai ke³.

