''Néi m ''hò t''iú-hak ngau-tsöng², hok₂ fán t''in shòng² tei² ha², kung² tei² ha² shuí chung kok mat₂-ke''yong²-tsz. Néi m ''hò pai¹ k''öü, yi-''ch''e fuk₂-sz² k''öü : yan-wai² Ngo, Ye-wo-wa, hai² nei-ke Shan, pat, yung néi pai pit₂ ko Shan, tsang Ngo-ke [''ngo tsau²] fat₂ k''öü-ke tsui², tsz² tsó-fu² to² tsz-sün sám sz toi²; oi'' Ngo-ke'', shan ngo kai ke'', tsau² shi-yan kwo'' k''öü to ts''in pák.toi².''

Tai² sám kai².

''Néi m hò lün* kiú néi Shan

Ye-wò-wá-ke meng*†, lün* kiú

ke'', Ye-wò-wá shi²-pit, ting² k''öü

tsui².

The Ten Commandments.

The First Commandment.—

God said, ''Excepting me beyond, you not good have another God.''

The Second Commandment.—

''You not good carve images, copying (or in imitation of) heaven above, earth below, and earth below water midst (i.e. that is in the water) any thing''s fashion: you not good worship them, moreover serve them: because I, Jehovah, am your God, not allow (or permit) you to worship another [C.] God. Hate me those [I then] punish their guilt or sin, from ancestors to descendants third fourth generations; love me those, observe my command ment those, then show mercy to them until thousand hundred generations.''

The Third Commandment.—

