Joseph separated-from Hebron went to Shechem that place, not find able arrive (i.e. the finding did not arrive at the conclusion wished for) brothers. That period have [C.] man say to-him to-hear, ''Your brothers gone have Dothan place; at that place find able right them.''

There-were several brothers seeing Joseph coming, then so said, ''The dreamer is-coming, 32; kill him; 21, throw his corpse down pit place; wait-till go home until say to father to-hear, say, there-was one [C.] fierce animal eat have him; afterwards see a-bit his dreaming matters have fulfilment (or) not.''

Reuben said, ''Do-not kill him, throw him down-into this pit place.'' Reuben not with those brothers so black heart. He wished to-place him down-into the-pit place, (and) wait-till each brother had-walked off that period-of time, then take him back out come, hand back-again-to (his) father.

Joseph come arrived that time, his those brothers caught him, tookoff his [C.] flowered coat, threw him down-into pit place. Very fortunate that pit no water at place, was dry.', 'Yök-shat,léi-hoiHéi-pak-lunhuitoShi²-kim''ko''shu'',mwantak''tohing-tai².Ko''chan²yauko''yanwa²k''öüt''eng†,''Néihing-tai²hui''hiúTo-tánshu'',haiko''shu''wantak,chok.k''öü.''Yaukéiko''hing-tai²''t''aikín''Yök₂-shatlaí-''kan,tsau²''komwá²,''Ko''fat₀-mung²-ke''laí-''kanlok₀;shát₀k''öüla;wingk''öüshilok₁hángshu'';tanghui¹kwaichi''wá²kwo''fú²-ts''ant''eng†,wá²,yauyatchek₀ok₀shau''shik₂hiúk''öü;hau²-loi''t''aihák''öüfát₀mung²tisz²yauying²-yim²mò.''Lau-pín²wá²,''M''hòshát.k''öü,wingk''öülokni-kohángshu².Lau-pín²mt''ungko²-tihing-tai²kòmhaksam.K''öüsòngchaik''öülokhángshu²,tangkok.hing-tai²hánghoíkochan²shí,tsaú²lok''öüfánch''utlaí,káu-wuifú²-ts''an.Yök-shat,laíto''ko''shi,k''öütihing-tai²chuk.(orchuk.)''tok''öü,ch''ük''öükin²fashám,wingk''öülok.hángshu''.''Hòts''oíko''hángmòshuihaíshu'',hai²konke''.Josephseparated-fromHebronwenttoShechemthatplace,notfindablearrive(i.e.thefindingdidnotarriveattheconclusionwishedfor)brothers.Thatperiodhave[C.]mansayto-himto-hear,''YourbrothersgonehaveDothanplace;atthatplacefindablerightthem.''There-wereseveralbrothersseeingJosephcoming,thensosaid,''Thedreameris-coming,32;killhim;21,throwhiscorpsedownpitplace;wait-tillgohomeuntilsaytofatherto-hear,say,there-wasone[C.]fierceanimaleathavehim;afterwardsseea-bithisdreamingmattershavefulfilment(or)not.''Reubensaid,''Do-notkillhim,throwhimdown-intothispitplace.''Reubennotwiththosebrotherssoblackheart.Hewishedto-placehimdown-intothe-pitplace,(and)wait-tilleachbrotherhad-walkedoffthatperiod-oftime,thentakehimbackoutcome,handback-again-to(his)father.Josephcomearrivedthattime,histhosebrotherscaughthim,tookoffhis[C.]floweredcoat,threwhimdown-intopitplace.Veryfortunatethatpitnowateratplace,wasdry.', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-076-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 76, 1, NULL, 'When his brothers had thrown him into the pit, they sat down and had their lunch. It was great pity they did this; it was because they hated their little brother Joseph that they did so. * * *.

採佢落坑個時,個啲兄弟坐倒地處食晏,可惜佢哋做呢啲事,因爲憎個細佬約瑟咋。

While Joseph''s brothers were eating, they looked up and saw a great many people coming. These people were the descendants of Ismael the son of Hagar. They came from Gilead, riding on camels, and brought many spices with them to take down into Egypt to sell.

約瑟兄弟食緊晏個時,擔高頭,見好多人嚟緊處,呢啲人係夏甲個仔,以實馬利嘅仔孫,喺基列處騎駱駝嚟到嘅,帶定好多香料,想拎去埃及處賣。

When Judah saw these people coming, he said to his brothers, ''Let us sell Joseph to these men.'' His brothers were pleased and took Joseph out of the pit at once, and sold him for twenty pieces of gold, which would now be worth about ten or eleven dollars.

猶大見呢啲人嚟緊處,就話過兄弟知,約瑟揩嚟賣過佢啲人,就着咯,佢啲兄弟話好,就即時喺坑處拉個約瑟上嚟,賣曉二十金,即係今日十零個銀錢。

The Ishmaelites took Joseph to Egypt and sold him to Potiphar. Reuben was not there when his brothers sold Joseph. When he came back he wanted to find Joseph; he was unable to find him; he was very sad, and tore his clothes.

