  ('rcc-080-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 80, 1, NULL, 'Yet he liked Daniel very much; and he set him over all the other judges and lords, and told all the people to mind him. Daniel was a very wise old man, and he was fit to be a judge. There were a great many rich men, who hated Daniel, because the King told them to mind Daniel, and because the King liked him better than them. These men were envious of Daniel. * * *.

但佢好歡喜個但以理,立佢做國中至大嘅官,吩咐衆人要聽佢教訓,但以理個陣時係老大,又好多智慧,有好多個啲財主人就好憎但以理,因爲個王呌佢哋聽但以理吩咐,又因爲個王歡喜但以理多過佢哋,噉佢就生個啲妒忌嘅心。* * *

These wicked rich men wished to hurt Daniel, and to get him into disgrace with King Darius; but they did not know how to get him into disgrace; they never saw Daniel do anything wrong. I suppose they were afraid of telling the King lies of Daniel, lest they should be found out. But at last they thought of a way to get Daniel into disgrace. They knew that he prayed very often to his God.

呢啲惡嘅財主人,想難爲但以理,又想令大利烏王唔歡喜佢,但係佢唔知揾乜野法子正做得,因佢唔察出但以理有乜野做錯嘅,佢哋收尾想出一個法子,會令大利烏王唔歡喜但以理咯,佢哋知到但以理一日之間好多賬要拜神嘅。

So they went to the King and asked him to make a law, that no one should pray to any God or man, but to the King himself, for thirty days.

佢哋就嚟求個王出命令,吩咐衆人三十日咁耐,樣樣嘅神都唔准佢哋拜,淨係拜個王咋。', 'YethelikedDanielverymuch;andhesethimoveralltheotherjudgesandlords,andtoldallthepeopletomindhim.Danielwasaverywiseoldman,andhewasfittobeajudge.Therewereagreatmanyrichmen,whohatedDaniel,becausetheKingtoldthemtomindDaniel,andbecausetheKinglikedhimbetterthanthem.ThesemenwereenviousofDaniel.***.但佢好歡喜個但以理,立佢做國中至大嘅官,吩咐衆人要聽佢教訓,但以理個陣時係老大,又好多智慧,有好多個啲財主人就好憎但以理,因爲個王呌佢哋聽但以理吩咐,又因爲個王歡喜但以理多過佢哋,噉佢就生個啲妒忌嘅心。***ThesewickedrichmenwishedtohurtDaniel,andtogethimintodisgracewithKingDarius;buttheydidnotknowhowtogethimintodisgrace;theyneversawDanieldoanythingwrong.IsupposetheywereafraidoftellingtheKingliesofDaniel,lesttheyshouldbefoundout.ButatlasttheythoughtofawaytogetDanielintodisgrace.TheyknewthatheprayedveryoftentohisGod.呢啲惡嘅財主人,想難爲但以理,又想令大利烏王唔歡喜佢,但係佢唔知揾乜野法子正做得,因佢唔察出但以理有乜野做錯嘅,佢哋收尾想出一個法子,會令大利烏王唔歡喜但以理咯,佢哋知到但以理一日之間好多賬要拜神嘅。SotheywenttotheKingandaskedhimtomakealaw,thatnooneshouldpraytoanyGodorman,buttotheKinghimself,forthirtydays.佢哋就嚟求個王出命令,吩咐衆人三十日咁耐,樣樣嘅神都唔准佢哋拜,淨係拜個王咋。', 'needs_review'),
