But he (was) very pleased-with that Daniel; appointed him to be country''s midst greatest officials, directed all men must obey his instructions. Daniel at-that [C.] time was old, had very much wisdom. There-were very many-of those wealthy men just much hated Daniel, because the King told them to-obey Daniel, (giving) directions further because the King was-pleased-with Daniel more than with-them. So they then grew those envious hearts. * * *.

These wicked wealthy men wished to oppress Daniel, also they-wished to cause Darius King not to-be-pleased-with him; but they (did) not know to-find what means properly to-do to-be-able; because they not find able out Daniel had what thing doing wrong. They finally thought out one [C.] means, (which) could cause Darius King not to-be-pleased-with Daniel, 32. They knew Daniel one day''s course very many times would pray-to God.

They then came (and) begged the King to-issue a-decree, directing all men thirty days so long within every kind of God also not to-allow them to-pray-to. Only to-pray-to the King only.', 'Tán²k''öühòfün-''heikoTán²-yi-lei;lap,k''öütso²kwok.chungchi''tai²kekwún,fan-fuchungyanyiút''eng†k''öükau''-fan''.Tán²-yi-leikochan²shíhai²lo-''tai*'',yau²hòtochi''-wai².Yauhòtoko''-tits''oi-chüyantsau²hòtsangTán²-yi-''lei,yan-wai²ko''wongkiù''k''öü-tei²t''eng†Tán²-yi-''leifan-fú'',yau²yan-wai²ko''wongfün-heiTán²-yi-''leitokwo''k''öü-tei².Komk''öütsau²shángko''-tito³-kei²ke''sam.***.Ni-tiok.ke''ts''oi-''chüyan''songnán-wai²Tán²-''yi-''lei,yau²''songling²Tai²-lei²-wuwongmfün-''heik''öü;tán²-hai²k''öümchí''wanmat,-yefát.-tszching''tso²tak;yank''öümch''atakch''utTán²-yi-leiyaumat,yetso²ts''o''ke''.K''öü-tei²shau-méi''songch''utyatko''fát.-tsz,wuiling²Tai²-lei²-wuwongmfún-''heiTán²-yi-leilok.K''öü-tei²chitoTán²-yi-leiyat,yat,chikänhotochong''yiúpaiShanke''.K''öü-téi²tsau²lai²k''auko²wongch''ut,ming²-ling²,fan-fu²chung²yansám-shap²yat²kom²noi²,yöng²-yöng²ke²Shantom''chun²k''öü-téi²pai²,tsing²hai²pai²ko²wongche.Buthe(was)verypleased-withthatDaniel;appointedhimtobecountry''smidstgreatestofficials,directedallmenmustobeyhisinstructions.Danielat-that[C.]timewasold,hadverymuchwisdom.There-wereverymany-ofthosewealthymenjustmuchhatedDaniel,becausetheKingtoldthemto-obeyDaniel,(giving)directionsfurtherbecausetheKingwas-pleased-withDanielmorethanwith-them.Sotheythengrewthoseenvioushearts.***.ThesewickedwealthymenwishedtooppressDaniel,alsothey-wishedtocauseDariusKingnotto-be-pleased-withhim;butthey(did)notknowto-findwhatmeansproperlyto-doto-be-able;becausetheynotfindableoutDanielhadwhatthingdoingwrong.Theyfinallythoughtoutone[C.]means,(which)couldcauseDariusKingnotto-be-pleased-withDaniel,32.TheyknewDanieloneday''scourseverymanytimeswouldpray-toGod.Theythencame(and)beggedtheKingto-issuea-decree,directingallmenthirtydayssolongwithineverykindofGodalsonotto-allowthemto-pray-to.Onlyto-pray-totheKingonl