  ('rcc-082-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 82, 1, NULL, 'And that if any one did pray to any one else, he should be cast into a den of lions. Now the King did not know why these men asked him to make this law: if the King had known that Daniel always prayed to his God, I do not think he would have made this law, for the King loved Daniel.

或有拜第二位,就要採佢入個啲獅竇處嘅。個王唔知爲乜呢啲人呌佢出噉嘅命令。我估或佢知到但以理日日噉多賬拜神,佢就唔會出噉嘅命令,因爲佢好愛但以理嘅。

The King was so foolish as to say that he would do as these men wished, because, you know, the King was a heathen, and he did not love the true God. * * *

但可惜個王唔係愛個位眞嘅神,佢係拜菩薩嘅。* * *

Daniel heard of the law that the King had made.

但以理聽聞個王出噉嘅命令。

Do you think that he went on praying?

佢都照舊一樣拜神嘅。

Daniel would have thought it very dreadful not to pray to God for thirty days. He wanted to praise God very often, and ask Him to bless him.

但以理點得三十日咁耐唔多謝,唔讚美神嘅恩典呢。

He used always to pray before the open window in his room. Perhaps you wonder why he did so. The reason was, he liked to look towards the place where he knew Jerusalem was. He could not see Jerusalem from his window, because it was so very far off; but still he knew which way it was, and he knew that God loved Jerusalem. * * *

佢時時都係喺自己房,打開度窗噉嚟拜嘅,佢噉做係因佢好愛耶路撒冷個城,佢就歡喜俾面向住個城嚟拜,佢唔睇見個耶路撒冷城,因爲隔得遠,但佢知到個城喺邊便,佢又知到神都好愛個城。* * *', 'Andthatifanyonedidpraytoanyoneelse,heshouldbecastintoadenoflions.NowtheKingdidnotknowwhythesemenaskedhimtomakethislaw:iftheKinghadknownthatDanielalwaysprayedtohisGod,Idonotthinkhewouldhavemadethislaw,fortheKinglovedDaniel.或有拜第二位,就要採佢入個啲獅竇處嘅。個王唔知爲乜呢啲人呌佢出噉嘅命令。我估或佢知到但以理日日噉多賬拜神,佢就唔會出噉嘅命令,因爲佢好愛但以理嘅。TheKingwassofoolishastosaythathewoulddoasthesemenwished,because,youknow,theKingwasaheathen,andhedidnotlovethetrueGod.***但可惜個王唔係愛個位眞嘅神,佢係拜菩薩嘅。***DanielheardofthelawthattheKinghadmade.但以理聽聞個王出噉嘅命令。Doyouthinkthathewentonpraying?佢都照舊一樣拜神嘅。DanielwouldhavethoughtitverydreadfulnottopraytoGodforthirtydays.HewantedtopraiseGodveryoften,andaskHimtoblesshim.但以理點得三十日咁耐唔多謝,唔讚美神嘅恩典呢。Heusedalwaystopraybeforetheopenwindowinhisroom.Perhapsyouwonderwhyhedidso.Thereasonwas,helikedtolooktowardstheplacewhereheknewJerusalemwas.HecouldnotseeJerusalemfromhiswindow,becauseitwassoveryfaroff;butstillheknewwhichwayitwas,andheknewthatGodlovedJerusalem.***佢時時都係喺自己房,打開度窗噉嚟拜嘅,佢噉做係因佢好愛耶路撒冷個城,佢就歡喜俾面向住個城嚟拜,佢唔睇見個耶路撒冷城,因爲隔得遠,但佢知到個城喺邊便,佢又知到神都好愛個城。***', 'needs_review');

