He constantly also did in his own room throw open [C.] window in that way in order to pray. He so did because he very loved Jerusalem that city. He then pleased to-put (his) face facing that city in-order-to pray. He not see that Jerusalem city, because separated able far; but he knew the city at what side. He also knew God very loved the city. * * *.', 'Wak,yaupaïtai²-yi²wai*,tsau²yiúwing,k''öüyapko-tisz-taushü.Ko,wongmchiwai²-matni-tiyankiù,k''öüch''ut,kom-keming²-ling.Ngokwuwak,k''öüchi-toTán²-yi-leiyat-yat,kömtochōngpaiShan,k''öütsau²mwuich''ut,kom-keming²-ling.yan-wai²k''öühooiTán²-yi-leike.Iftherewaspraying-toanother[C.],thenmustthrowhimintothoselions''denplace.TheKingnotknowwhythesementoldhimto-issuesuchdecree.IthinkifheknewDanieldailysomanytimesprayed-toGod,hethennotwould-haveissuedsucha-decree,becausehemuchlovedDaniel.Tân''ho-sikko''wongmhai²oiko''wai*chan-keShan,k''öühai²paip''o-saitke.***.Butitis-to-be-pitied-thattheKingnotdidlovethe[C.]trueGod.Hedidpraytoidols.***.Tán²-yi-leit''eng†-manko''wongch''ut,komkeming²-ling²Danielheard(that)theKinghad-issuedsuch-adecree.K''öütochiükan²yat,yöng²paiShanke.Healsoaccordingtoold(mannerortime)onesameprayedto-God.Tán²-yi-leitimtak,sám-shap,yat,kömnoi²,mto-tse²mtsán²-méiShanke''yan-tinni?Danielhowcouldthirtydayssolongnotthank(and)notpraiseGod''smercyeh?53.K''öüshi-shitohai²haitsz²-kéifong*ta-hoito²ch''ongkömlaipaike.K''öükómtsó²yank''öühòoiYe-lo²-sát·längko''sheng†.K''öütsau²fün-heipéimin²hòng-chüko''sheng†laipai.K''öümt''ai-kinko''Ye-lo²-sát·längsheng†,yan-wai²káktak''yun;tán²k''öüchi-toko''sheng†haipinpin².K''öüyauchi-toShanhôoiko''sheng†.***.Heconstantlyalsodidinhisownroomthrowopen[C.]windowinthatwayinordertopray.HesodidbecauseheverylovedJerusalemthatcity.Hethenpleasedto-put(his)facefacingthatcityin-order-topray.HenotseethatJerusalemcity,becauseseparatedablefar;butheknewthecityatwhatside.HealsoknewGodverylovedthecity.***.', 'verified'),
  ('rcc-084-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 84, 1, NULL, 'So Daniel liked to look that way when he prayed. He knelt down three times every day, and prayed, and thanked God for all His kindness to him.

噉佢歡喜面向個便嚟拜,佢日日三賬都係噉跪倒個處嚟拜神,多謝神咁大恩典待佢。而家出曉個命令,佢都係照一樣噉拜。

The men who hated Daniel heard that he went on praying: so they went one day to look at him praying, that they might tell the King that they had seen him.

個啲憎但以理嘅人,聽聞佢照舊噉拜,佢哋一日知到係佢拜嘅時候,就去賍佢,等佢哋做得話個王知,係佢哋親眼見佢拜。

Then they asked the King, ''Did you not make a law that if any one prayed to any god or man, excepting you, that he should be cast into a den of lions?''

佢哋就嚟對個王話,你唔係出曉一個命令,或者一個人三十日咁耐,有拜神,唔係獨拜你,就要採佢落獅竇。

And the King said, ''Yes, it is true, and I cannot change the law.''

個王話,係眞嘅咯,我又唔改得呢個命令嘅。

Then the men said, ''That Daniel, who was brought from Jerusalem to be a slave, does not mind you, nor your law, but prays three times a day.''

個啲人就話,係即路撒冷帶嚟個但以理唔聽你嘅命令,一日之間,都三偏拜神。', 'SoDaniellikedtolookthatwaywhenheprayed.Hekneltdownthreetimeseveryday,andprayed,andthankedGodforallHiskindnesstohim.噉佢歡喜面向個便嚟拜,佢日日三賬都係噉跪倒個處嚟拜神,多謝神咁大恩典待佢。而家出曉個命令,佢都係照一樣噉拜。ThemenwhohatedDanielheardthathewentonpraying:sotheywentonedaytolookathimpraying,thattheymighttelltheKingthattheyhadseenhim.個啲憎但以理嘅人,聽聞佢照舊噉拜,佢哋一日知到係佢拜嘅時候,就去賍佢,等佢哋做得話個王知,係佢哋親眼見佢拜。ThentheyaskedtheKing,''Didyounotmakealawthatifanyoneprayedtoanygodorman,exceptingyou,thatheshouldbecastintoadenoflions?''佢哋就嚟對個王話,你唔係出曉一個命令,或者一個人三十日咁耐,有拜神,唔係獨拜你,就要採佢落獅竇。AndtheKingsaid,''Yes,itistrue,andIcannotchangethelaw.''個王話,係眞嘅咯,我又唔改得呢個命令嘅。Thenthemensaid,''ThatDaniel,whowasbroughtfromJerusalemtobeaslave,doesnotmindyou,noryourlaw,butpraysthreetimesaday.''個啲人就話,係即路撒冷帶嚟個但以理唔聽你嘅命令,一日之間,都三偏拜神。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-085-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 85, 1, NULL, 'Kòm k''öü fún-''héi mín² hög'' ko pín² laí pai''. K''öü yat²-yat² sám chòng''tó haï² kòm kwai²-tò ko shü'' laí pai'' Shan, to-tse² Shan kòm tái² yan-tín, toi² k''öü. Yi-ká ch''ut, hiú ko'' ming²-ling'', k''öü to hai² chiú yat, yöng'' kòm pai''

So he was-pleased (to have his) face towards that side in-order-to pray. He day (by) day three times also did so kneel-at that place in-order-to pray to-God to-thank God such great grace towards him. Now issued had the decree, he also did according-to one same so pray.

Ko''-ti tsang Tán²-yi-léi ke'' yan t''eng†-man k''öü chiú'' kan² kòm pai'': k''öü-tei² yat, yat, chí-to'' hai² k''öü pai''-ke'' shí-hau² tsau² huí'' chong k''öü, tang k''öü-tei² tsò-tak wá'' ko'' wong chi, haí² k''öü-tei² ts''an ngán kin'' k''öü pai''

Those (who) hated Daniel people heard he according-to old (time) so prayed: they one day knew it-was his praying time then went to-spy-on him so-that they do could say-to the King to-know it was they with-their-owned eyes saw him pray.

K''öü-tei² tsan² laí tuì'' ko'' wong wá'', Néi m haï² ch''ut, hiú yat, ko'' ming²-ling'', wák''-che yat, ko'' yan sám-shap² yat, kòm noi², yau pai'' Shan, m haï² tuk pai'' néi, tsan² yiu'' wing k''öü lok'' sz-tau''

They then came (and) to the King said, ''You not have (i.e. Have you not) issued done a [C.] decree (to the effect that), if a [C.] man (for the space of) thirty days so long did pray to-God, (and) not did only pray to-you, then must thrown down lions'' den?''

