Afterwards he grown-up, then went allround (every where) did very many wonderfnl things, to-reveal (display make clear) out his power.', 'To³hop₂shi-hau²ko²chan²shi,Ye-sòtsan²houszyatko²sò-tsaikomkongshangshai-kán.K''öüch''utshaihaihaiYan-t''aiShángyattiùts''unkot''iuts''unkiútsòPak-lér²hang.Hau²-loik''öütai²-hiu,tsan²hünchau-waits²hotoch''ut-k''eikesz²,hinch''utk''öü-kek''un-nang.Arrivedpropertimethat[C.]time,Jesusthenverylikeone[C.]babysodescend-intolife(inthe)world''smidst.Hiscoming-out-intotheworldwasinJudaeaProvinceone[C.]village,that[C.]villagecalledto-beBethlehem.Afterwardshegrown-up,thenwentallround(everywhere)didverymanywonderfnlthings,to-reveal(displaymakeclear)outhispower.', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-094-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 94, 1, NULL, 'He once met a man who had been born blind. Jesus pitied him and cured him, so that he was able to see at once.

He also made the lame, whom he met and who had been ill for many years, quite well again.

Jesus did not heal the sick, as the doctors do, by giving them medicine to cure them: he just said a few words, telling them to be well immediately, and they were well at once.

The sick that came to Jesus are to be counted by the thousands, and not by the hundreds. It did not matter what the sickness was, Jesus made them well.

Besides this Jesus did a great many wonderful things: he caused the dead to rise again.

There was once a girl who was dead. Her father and mother were very sad, and very distressed about it; but, when Jesus came, he immediately told her to come to life again.

Again there was a poor widow woman whose only son had died, and when they were carrying him away to bury him, Jesus met them on the street.

佢有一回，遇着一個人，出世就盲曉眼嘅，耶穌可憐佢，就醫好佢，令佢即時睇得見。

又遇着啲跛腳嘅，遠年患病嘅，都即時令佢哋好翻。

耶穌即醫好人，唔係同啲醫生配藥材嚟醫嘅，係出一句說話，叫即時好翻，個嘅人就好翻嘅咯。

講千唔講百咁多病人嚟到耶穌處，唔論乜野病，耶穌都醫翻好佢。

耶穌又做過好多至出奇嘅事添，即係令個嘅死曉嘅人翻生。

有一回，有個女仔已經死曉嘅咯，佢嘅父母好閉翳，好淒涼，即耶穌嚟到，就即時叫佢翻生。

又有個貧窮嘅寡母婆，死曉一個孤獨仔，抬去葬之時，耶穌喺街遇着佢。', 'Heoncemetamanwhohadbeenbornblind.Jesuspitiedhimandcuredhim,sothathewasabletoseeatonce.Healsomadethelame,whomhemetandwhohadbeenillformanyyears,quitewellagain.Jesusdidnothealthesick,asthedoctorsdo,bygivingthemmedicinetocurethem:hejustsaidafewwords,tellingthemtobewellimmediately,andtheywerewellatonce.ThesickthatcametoJesusaretobecountedbythethousands,andnotbythehundreds.Itdidnotmatterwhatthesicknesswas,Jesusmadethemwell.BesidesthisJesusdidagreatmanywonderfulthings:hecausedthedeadtoriseagain.Therewasonceagirlwhowasdead.Herfatherandmotherwereverysad,andverydistressedaboutit;but,whenJesuscame,heimmediatelytoldhertocometolifeagain.Againtherewasapoorwidowwomanwhoseonlysonhaddied,andwhentheywerecarryinghimawaytoburyhim,Jesusmetthemonthestreet.佢有一回，遇着一個人，出世就盲曉眼嘅，耶穌可憐佢，就醫好佢，令佢即時睇得見。又遇着啲跛腳嘅，遠年患病嘅，都即時令佢哋好翻。耶穌即醫好人，唔係同啲醫生配藥材嚟醫嘅，係出一句說話，叫即時好翻，個嘅人就好翻嘅咯。講千唔講百咁多病人嚟到耶穌處，唔論乜野病，耶穌都醫翻好佢。耶穌又做過好多至出奇嘅事添，即係令個嘅死曉嘅人翻生。有一回，有個女仔已經死曉嘅咯，佢嘅父母好閉翳，好淒涼，即耶穌嚟到，就即時叫佢翻生。又有個貧窮嘅寡母婆，死曉一個孤獨仔，抬去葬之時，耶穌喺街遇着佢。', 'needs_review'),
