  ('rcc-096-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 96, 1, NULL, 'He went up to the side of the corpse and told the dead man to rise, and the only son at once came to life again. When the widow woman saw her son come to life again, she was very happy.

There was another dead man whose name was Lazarus. He had been buried for four days; but Jesus went to the grave and called him back to life again; and he came out of the tomb at once. * * *

There was still one thing that he did besides. That was the best; so I must tell you about it; it is healing very serious illness.

What illness is that? It is a disease of the heart: it is sin. That illness you, I, and every one have; but if we can have him say, ''Your sins are forgiven''—if every could hear those words, they would certainly be glad and would have no more sickness.

If anyone comes and asks him now to heal him, he will not say he is unwilling to do so; and when he heals people, he does not take their money, so the poor and the rich can come to him.—''The Sweet Story of the Cross.''

就埋去叫佢起身，個孤獨仔即時就翻生咯，當時個寡母婆見個仔翻生，就十分歡喜咯。

又有一個死人，名叫拉撒路，已經葬曉四日咯，耶穌去墳墓處叫佢翻生，佢即由墳墓翻出嚟。＊＊＊

佢重有一樣事做出添，個樣係至好嘅事，故此我要講過你哋知，即係醫好人哋好關係嘅病症咯。

