  ('rcc-106-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 106, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>He is present with us at night the same as during the day. Whether at home or abroad, it is all the same: his eye does not sleep.</td><td>佢夜晚同埋我哋係好似日頭一樣。我哋出外好似喺屋企一樣，佢嘅眼唔瞓。</td></tr><tr><td>His arm is always strong. There is no place where he is not. In the Psalms, it is said, ‘God is our refuge and strength; a very present help in trouble.’ David also said, ‘The Lord is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?’</td><td>佢手時時有力，無地不在。聖書詩篇有話，我哋當患難時，神極力嚟幫助。大闢都話，神係幫助我，我使慌乜野呢。</td></tr><tr><td>Long ago David kept his flock of sheep; and a lion and a bear tried to get his sheep; but David was not afraid, because God helped him to kill those two fierce beasts. He was not even afraid of Goliath the Philistine, though he was a giant and a fierce man of war, because God helped him and caused him to vanquish Goliath. Everyone in this world, whoever he is, requires God to help him.</td><td>昔日大闢牧羊羣，有一隻獅，一隻熊，想捉佢嘅羊，但大闢唔怕，因爲神幫助佢打死個兩隻惡獸，佢都唔怕非利士人烏利亞高大勇猛，因爲神幫助，令佢打贏烏利亞。世界中所有嘅人，一切要神幫助。</td></tr><tr><td>The Gentiles have many gods. They think one god attends to one place, and cannot help the people belonging to another place; but this is not wise, it is foolish.</td><td>異邦人有好多神，佢估一位神打理一笪地方，唔幫助得第二處嘅人，但呢啲唔係聰明嘅，係愚蠢啫。</td></tr><tr><td>Truly the gods of the Gentiles, no matter of what place, are not able to help their suppliants. No man, who ever he may be, is able to help us.</td><td>眞講異邦人嘅神，唔論邊笪，不能幫助所求佢嘅，唔論乜人都唔幫助得。</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>Heispresentwithusatnightthesameasduringtheday.Whetherathomeorabroad,itisallthesame:hiseyedoesnotsleep.</td><td>佢夜晚同埋我哋係好似日頭一樣。我哋出外好似喺屋企一樣，佢嘅眼唔瞓。</td></tr><tr><td>Hisarmisalwaysstrong.Thereisnoplacewhereheisnot.InthePsalms,itissaid,‘Godisourrefugeandstrength;averypresenthelpintrouble.’Davidalsosaid,‘TheLordisthestrengthofmylife;ofwhomshallIbeafraid?’</td><td>佢手時時有力，無地不在。聖書詩篇有話，我哋當患難時，神極力嚟幫助。大闢都話，神係幫助我，我使慌乜野呢。</td></tr><tr><td>LongagoDavidkepthisflockofsheep;andalionandabeartriedtogethissheep;butDavidwasnotafraid,becauseGodhelpedhimtokillthosetwofiercebeasts.HewasnotevenafraidofGoliaththePhilistine,thoughhewasagiantandafiercemanofwar,becauseGodhelpedhimandcausedhimtovanquishGoliath.Everyoneinthisworld,whoeverheis,requiresGodtohelphim.</td><td>昔日大闢牧羊羣，有一隻獅，一隻熊，想捉佢嘅羊，但大闢唔怕，因爲神幫助佢打死個兩隻惡獸，佢都唔怕非利士人烏利亞高大勇猛，因爲神幫助，令佢打贏烏利亞。世界中所有嘅人，一切要神幫助。</td></tr><tr><td>TheGentileshavemanygods.Theythinkonegodattendstooneplace,andcannothelpthepeoplebelongingtoanotherplace;butthisisnotwise,itisfoolish.</td><td>異邦人有好多神，佢估一位神打理一笪地方，唔幫助得第二處嘅人，但呢啲唔係聰明嘅，係愚蠢啫。</td></tr><tr><td>TrulythegodsoftheGentiles,nomatterofwhatplace,arenotabletohelptheirsuppliants.Noman,whoeverhemaybe,isabletohelpus.</td><td>眞講異邦人嘅神，唔論邊笪，不能幫助所求佢嘅，唔論乜人都唔幫助得。</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
