  ('rcc-124-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 124, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>When Thou hadst overcome the sharpness of death, Thou didst open the kingdom of heaven to all believers.
Thou sittest at the right hand of God, in the glory of the Father.</td><td>主呀,你打勝死亡之後,就爲一切信道人開曉天國之門。
主呀,你坐在上主之右邊,享受聖父之榮耀。</td></tr><tr><td>We believe that Thou shalt come to be our Judge.
We therefore pray Thee, help Thy servants, whom Thou hast redeemed with Thy precious blood.
Make them to be numbered with Thy saints in glory everlasting.</td><td>我哋信主,必再降臨審問我哋。
主呀,你曾用寶血贖救世人,我哋現在求主拯救。
使我哋得列在聖徒之中,得享永遠榮耀。</td></tr><tr><td>O Lord, save Thy people, and bless thine heritage.</td><td>主呀,我哋求主拯救主之百姓,賜福俾主之選民。</td></tr><tr><td>Govern them, and lift them up for ever.
Day by day, we magnify Thee;
And we worship Thy name, ever world without end.
Vonchsafe, O Lord, to keep us this day without sin.
O Lord, have mercy upon us, have mercy upon us.
O Lord, let Thy mercy lighten upon us, as our trust is in Thee.
O Lord, in Thee have I trusted: Let me never be confounded.</td><td>求主常常管束我哋,扶助我哋。
