  ('rcc-128-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 128, 1, 'LESSON, XXV.', 'And Ruth the Moabitess said unto Naomi, ''Let me now go to the field, and glean among the ears of corn after him in whose sight I shall find grace.'' And she said unto her, ''Go, my daughter.'' And she went, and came and gleaned in the field after the reapers: and her hap was to light on the portion of the field belonging unto Boaz, * * *. And, behold, Boaz came from Bethlehem, and said unto the reapers, ''The Lord be with you.'' And they answered him, ''The Lord bless thee.'' * * * .

Then said Boaz unto Ruth, ''Hearest thou not, my daughter? Go not to glean in another field, neither pass from hence, but abide here fast by my maidens. Let thine eyes be on the field that they do reap, and go thou after them: Have I not charged the young men that they shall not touch thee? And when thou art athirst, go unto the vessels, and drink of that which the young men have drawn.''

摩押女路得對拿阿咪話,我想去田間,若係(我)得乜誰嘅恩,(我)就喺(啁)個人後便執佢剩下嘅麥穗。拿阿咪答話,媳婦呀,只管去喇。路得就去到田間,跟住收割嘅人,執佢剩下嘅穗,佢所到嘅田,剛啱係波士嘅。* * *波士正從伯利恒嚟,對割禾嘅人話,願耶和華同埋你哋,眾人答話,願耶和華賜福過你。* * *

波士對路得話,我女呀,你聽我講,唔使(or 好)去別人嘅田執遺穗,咪離開呢處,惟係近埋我嘅婢女喺呢處喇。佢哋住喺邊笪田,你就跟住佢哋去,我已經吩咐少年人咪欺負你,若係你渴就去佢哋器皿飲僕人所汲嘅水。', 'AndRuththeMoabitesssaiduntoNaomi,''Letmenowgotothefield,andgleanamongtheearsofcornafterhiminwhosesightIshallfindgrace.''Andshesaiduntoher,''Go,mydaughter.''Andshewent,andcameandgleanedinthefieldafterthereapers:andherhapwastolightontheportionofthefieldbelonginguntoBoaz,***.And,behold,BoazcamefromBethlehem,andsaiduntothereapers,''TheLordbewithyou.''Andtheyansweredhim,''TheLordblessthee.''***.ThensaidBoazuntoRuth,''Hearestthounot,mydaughter?Gonottogleaninanotherfield,neitherpassfromhence,butabideherefastbymymaidens.Letthineeyesbeonthefieldthattheydoreap,andgothouafterthem:HaveInotchargedtheyoungmenthattheyshallnottouchthee?Andwhenthouartathirst,gountothevessels,anddrinkofthatwhichtheyoungmenhavedrawn.''摩押女路得對拿阿咪話,我想去田間,若係(我)得乜誰嘅恩,(我)就喺(啁)個人後便執佢剩下嘅麥穗。拿阿咪答話,媳婦呀,只管去喇。路得就去到田間,跟住收割嘅人,執佢剩下嘅穗,佢所到嘅田,剛啱係波士嘅。***波士正從伯利恒嚟,對割禾嘅人話,願耶和華同埋你哋,眾人答話,願耶和華賜福過你。***波士對路得話,我女呀,你聽我講,唔使(or好)去別人嘅田執遺穗,咪離開呢處,惟係近埋我嘅婢女喺呢處喇。佢哋住喺邊笪田,你就跟住佢哋去,我已經吩咐少年人咪欺負你,若係你渴就去佢哋器皿飲僕人所汲嘅水。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-129-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 129, 1, 'LESSON, XXV.', 'Mò-ap. nöü Ló²-tak, toü. Ná-o-mai wá'', ''Ngo söng höü t''in-kán, yök hai² (ngo) tak mat shui* ke yan, (ngo) tsau² hai (''ko) ko yan hau² pin² chap, k''öü shing²-ha² ke mak² soü².'' Ná-o-mai táp wa², ''Sik-fú a'', chik-''kwúnhöü la.'' Lo²-tak tsau² höü to t''in-kán, kan-chü² shau-kot-ke²-yan, chap, k''öü shing²-ha² ke''soü²: k''öü ''sho to'' ke''tin, kong-ngámhai² Po-sz ke''. * * *. Po-sz ching ts''ung Pak-lei²-hang lai, toü kot-wo ke''yan wa², ''Yün² Ye-wo-wa t''ung-mái néi-tei².'' Chung² yan tap.wa², ''Yün² Ye-wo-wa t''sz fuk,kwo''néi.'' * * *.

Po-sz toü'' Lo²-tak wä², ''Ngo noü a'', nei t''eng† ngo kong. M shai (or ho)höü pit yan-ke t''in chap, wai söü²; mai lei-hoi ni shu'', wai hai² kan-mai ngo-ke''p''ei-nöü hai ni shu''là. K''öü-tei² chu''hai pint tát.t''in shau-kot, tsau² kan-chü² k''öü-tei²höü'': Ngo yí-king fän-fu'' shiú nín yan mai hei-fu² néi. Yok hai² néi hot, tsau²höü k''öü-tei² hei''ming, yam pnk-yan ''sho k''ap, ke''shuí.''

The Moabitess woman Ruth to Naomi said, ''I wish go field if (I) obtain anyone''s grace, (I) then at (that) [C.] man behind pick-up (what) he leaves-behind of wheat. Naomi answered, said, ''Daughter-in-law (it means also a grandson''s or nephew''s wife), 2,'' very-well-then go, 21. Ruth then went to (the) fields, followed reapers, picked-up they left-behind of ears-of-grain: she what arrived-at field exactly was Boaz''s. * * *. Boaz exactly from Bethlehem came, to cutters-of-grain-men said, ''I-wish Jehovah (be) together-with you.'' All the-people answered, said, ''May Jehovah bestow happiness upon you.'' * * *.

