  ('rcc-138-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 138, 1, NULL, 'they began to be hardened. They also thought to drive away his distemper by harsh and surly carriages to him: sometimes they would deride, sometimes they would chide, and sometimes they would quite neglect him. Wherefore he began to retire himself to his chamber, to pray for and pity them, and also to condole his own misery; he would also walk solitarily in the fields, sometimes reading, and sometimes praying: and thus for some days he spent his time.—''Bunyan''s Pilgrim''s Progress.''

搵昨日個啲說話，講過佢哋聽，佢哋總唔睬佢，意思以爲唔俾禮貌待佢，或者可以好翻，噉就又有時恥笑佢，或怒罵佢，或總唔理佢。所以佢自己入去房中，一則閉翳自己罪惡，一則可憐家人痴迷不醒，替佢哋祈禱。又每每獨自己（一個）出去田中，或睇書，或祈禱，一連幾日都係噉。', 'theybegantobehardened.Theyalsothoughttodriveawayhisdistemperbyharshandsurlycarriagestohim:sometimestheywouldderide,sometimestheywouldchide,andsometimestheywouldquiteneglecthim.Whereforehebegantoretirehimselftohischamber,toprayforandpitythem,andalsotocondolehisownmisery;hewouldalsowalksolitarilyinthefields,sometimesreading,andsometimespraying:andthusforsomedayshespenthistime.—''Bunyan''sPilgrim''sProgress.''搵昨日個啲說話，講過佢哋聽，佢哋總唔睬佢，意思以爲唔俾禮貌待佢，或者可以好翻，噉就又有時恥笑佢，或怒罵佢，或總唔理佢。所以佢自己入去房中，一則閉翳自己罪惡，一則可憐家人痴迷不醒，替佢哋祈禱。又每每獨自己（一個）出去田中，或睇書，或祈禱，一連幾日都係噉。', 'needs_review'),
