  ('rcc-208-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 208, 1, NULL, 'mother-in-law. Do you think it is a new thing to do? What is the use of your mincing walk, affected tones, ogling eyes, and expressive face? Do you, dressed up in that fascinating style, wish to come and woo me? When I was first a bride, I was ten times prettier than you are. I never thought that old age would now make me ugly and diminish my good looks.'' When Coral heard this, she hung down her head, and received the rebuke submissively without presuming to say a word.

Coral again, early the next morning, presented cakes and tea, and asked for her mother-in-law. She was dressed plainly though nicely, and looked neat and clean; she had on a washable, blue jacket; and had neither powdered nor rouged herself. As soon as Old Cross Sticks had set eyes on her, her ire again rose; and she greeted her with:—''I only said a word to you yesterday, and you come this morning then, without putting a flower in your hair, or powder on your face, or your best clothes on. You want to come and make me angry. Do you think I don''t know? Do you think I

你十倍,唔估今日老得個樣醜態減去三分。

